WEBVTT

00:43.770 --> 00:45.570
Hell yeah!

00:45.570 --> 00:48.310
Nailed it!

00:55.030 --> 00:56.170
Subaru.

00:57.420 --> 00:59.500
You've done well, I suppose.

01:00.580 --> 01:02.670
Yeah. Oh, and thanks.

01:05.920 --> 01:09.010
It's nice and cool.
I feel alive again!

01:09.010 --> 01:12.340
You should thank Petra directly.

01:12.340 --> 01:15.220
The girl would leap for joy, I suppose.

01:17.400 --> 01:20.390
To think it's been a year
since our pact, Bea-ko.

01:20.810 --> 01:24.900
Time flies by so fast,
but you're still as cute as ever.

01:24.900 --> 01:26.650
I'm really touched.

01:26.650 --> 01:30.790
He-he! Betty's cuteness is only a given!

01:30.790 --> 01:33.780
I've also bulked up a lot this past year!

01:33.780 --> 01:35.580
Pffft! I suppose.

01:35.580 --> 01:37.290
That was a good joke!

01:37.290 --> 01:39.770
Yes, perhaps a bit too funny, I wonder.

01:39.770 --> 01:42.120
Hey, I was being serious!

01:42.520 --> 01:45.920
Take a good look
at my secret training grounds!

01:46.450 --> 01:49.880
I can even perfectly clear
all those brutal attractions

01:49.880 --> 01:53.090
that'd make any grown-up cry now!

01:53.090 --> 01:55.090
Are you exaggerating, I wonder?

01:55.450 --> 02:00.850
I suppose you are, as you and Garfiel
are the only ones who call it "secret."

02:00.850 --> 02:03.900
- Now you've said it!
- Kyaaa! I suppose!

02:03.900 --> 02:05.400
Is this spirit abuse, I wonder?!

02:05.400 --> 02:07.860
What a heinous contractor!

02:07.860 --> 02:10.440
Master Subaru! Beatrice!

02:10.440 --> 02:13.150
We have guests at the mansion!

02:14.570 --> 02:17.700
Lady Emilia wants you to come with her!

02:18.370 --> 02:20.200
Unexpected visitors...

02:21.050 --> 02:23.750
And the cutie Emilia-tan
who's calling for me...

02:24.200 --> 02:26.030
I smell a case brewing!

02:26.030 --> 02:29.340
Something troublesome
is coming our way, I suppose.

02:30.000 --> 02:32.590
Woah, it's Mister!

02:32.590 --> 02:34.800
How've ya been?

02:36.800 --> 02:40.680
Mimi! It's been a while!
Doing great out there?

02:40.680 --> 02:42.730
Yeah! Mimi's doing super great!

02:42.730 --> 02:45.850
Also got taller!
Pretty much a grown woman now!

02:45.850 --> 02:49.480
What kind of grown woman jumps
on someone the moment they meet?!

02:50.400 --> 02:53.440
Anyway, you sure came a long way.

02:54.320 --> 02:56.950
Wait, if you're here, then...

02:56.950 --> 03:00.030
Don'tcha worry, Mister!

03:00.030 --> 03:03.000
Julius isn't with us today!

03:14.510 --> 03:16.470
You're finally here, Barusu.

03:16.470 --> 03:18.330
You're late.

03:20.100 --> 03:21.010
Indecent.

03:21.010 --> 03:22.390
No, you're indecent!

03:22.390 --> 03:24.730
How can you see this
as anything but wholesome?!

03:26.070 --> 03:30.230
Please stop basing everything
on your perspective.

03:30.820 --> 03:33.110
You'd best remember this, Barusu:

03:33.110 --> 03:35.700
In Ram's world,
only Ram's perspective matters.

03:35.700 --> 03:39.660
I swear you were contradicting yourself
just now!

03:39.660 --> 03:42.030
Yo! Ya sure took your time, Chief.

03:42.030 --> 03:43.930
Come on in.

03:43.930 --> 03:46.500
Watchin' my bro Otto and Lady Emilia
welcome our visitor

03:46.500 --> 03:48.540
ain't nothin' short of comedy!

03:48.540 --> 03:51.790
Now that's a performance
I want to see!

03:51.790 --> 03:53.960
Stop blabbering and get in.

04:00.640 --> 04:02.310
So this is...?

04:02.310 --> 04:03.930
Yes, that's correct.

04:03.930 --> 04:05.730
I'm sorry for the wait.

04:06.550 --> 04:09.560
This is my knight, Natsuki Subaru.

04:11.980 --> 04:14.190
"My knight"...!

04:15.750 --> 04:17.280
Is something the matter?

04:17.280 --> 04:20.030
Whoops, zoned out back there.

04:21.370 --> 04:23.410
Sorry about that.

04:26.000 --> 04:28.120
Allow me to introduce myself.

04:28.120 --> 04:31.460
I am Lady Emilia's knight, Natsuki Subaru.

04:32.960 --> 04:35.380
Thank you for your courtesy.

04:35.380 --> 04:36.390
I'm...

04:37.380 --> 04:40.760
I have come at the behest
of Anastasia Hoshin.

04:41.420 --> 04:43.550
My name is Joshua Juukulius.

04:44.890 --> 04:46.430
Juukulius?

04:46.850 --> 04:49.600
Ah, it seems you're surprised too, Subaru.

04:49.600 --> 04:53.690
That's right! Apparently,
Joshua is Julius' younger brother!

04:54.980 --> 04:56.730
Sir Natsuki, was it?

04:56.730 --> 05:01.410
I have heard about you from my brother...
as well as from other various rumors.

05:01.880 --> 05:04.740
Oh. Julius' younger brother, huh...?

05:04.740 --> 05:09.210
Now that you mention it,
that nasty... I mean, keen gaze,

05:09.210 --> 05:12.580
and that sarcas...
I mean, refined manner of speech,

05:12.580 --> 05:16.210
and that terribly... lovely hair color
and face are the same as his.

05:16.210 --> 05:19.550
Could you stop saying unnecessary things?
You're clearly struggling.

05:20.420 --> 05:25.220
Okay, sorry to make you wait.
Could we continue the conversation?

05:25.220 --> 05:27.010
Please wait a moment!

05:27.010 --> 05:28.180
Who is this girl?!

05:28.180 --> 05:30.480
Is something the matter
with Betty, I wonder?

05:30.480 --> 05:32.020
This is Bea-ko!

05:32.020 --> 05:34.610
It's Miss and Mister's kid!

05:35.690 --> 05:37.180
That's right!

05:37.180 --> 05:40.990
This is my and Emilia-tan's
adorable baby, Beatrice!

05:40.990 --> 05:42.490
Goodness, no.

05:42.490 --> 05:44.670
Look at how you've startled Joshua!

05:44.670 --> 05:48.830
We may have smooched,
but babies don't come from smooches!

05:48.830 --> 05:50.160
I know because I studied!

05:50.160 --> 05:52.210
Sorry, Emilia-tan.

05:52.210 --> 05:56.130
It's, uh, really embarrassing when you
give away details like that so bluntly.

05:56.130 --> 05:58.050
Please stop.
It's all my fault, okay?

05:58.050 --> 06:03.470
Um, might I inquire
about her actual position, then?

06:03.860 --> 06:07.350
Great Spirit Beatrice,
the cutie I've formed a pact with.

06:08.510 --> 06:10.310
A great spirit...

06:10.310 --> 06:12.060
So, esteemed guest,

06:12.060 --> 06:16.560
ya got a problem with the Chief
bringin' his spirit with him?

06:16.990 --> 06:19.730
No, I've heard the rumors,

06:19.730 --> 06:23.030
but you really are a spirit knight,
Sir Natsuki.

06:23.650 --> 06:27.490
I am sure you're already aware,
but my brother is also a spirit knight,

06:27.490 --> 06:30.290
previously the only one in the Kingdom!

06:30.290 --> 06:32.460
Yeah, of course I know that.

06:32.460 --> 06:38.290
He was a big pai...
big help, after all.

06:38.290 --> 06:41.260
Do you really hate admitting
he helped you that much?

06:41.700 --> 06:46.470
Betty is aware that there is another
spirit knight aside from Subaru.

06:46.470 --> 06:49.260
He must be a rather
remarkable individual, I suppose.

06:49.260 --> 06:52.850
Of course!
Lord Brother is an amazing person!

06:52.850 --> 06:54.690
At the young age of twenty-two,

06:54.690 --> 06:59.690
he is already the ace and essentially
the second-in-command of the Royal Guard!

06:59.690 --> 07:01.610
Though he's away from his duties,

07:02.040 --> 07:06.320
he's certain to become Captain
once Lady Anastasia ascends to the throne.

07:06.320 --> 07:08.870
Not even Sir Reinhard,
the current Sword Saint,

07:08.870 --> 07:11.620
can match my brother
in terms of knightly virtues.

07:11.620 --> 07:14.450
Lord Brother is truly
the epitome of knighthood!

07:14.450 --> 07:15.870
Sure...

07:15.870 --> 07:17.170
I am speechless.

07:18.000 --> 07:21.710
You really love your brother,
don't you, Joshua?

07:22.800 --> 07:24.670
M-My apologies!

07:24.670 --> 07:27.050
I lose control
when it comes to my family...

07:27.050 --> 07:30.260
Who cares? Get to the point.

07:30.260 --> 07:34.230
Even if the bambeem gets better over time,
there's gotta be a limit, ya know.

07:34.230 --> 07:36.060
Bambeem?

07:36.060 --> 07:38.520
Mimi loves those! They're yummy!

07:39.310 --> 07:40.860
Wanna eat some together?

07:40.860 --> 07:42.020
Uh, sure...

07:42.420 --> 07:44.400
It's a promise, 'kay?

07:46.470 --> 07:47.820
Apologies for the diversion.

07:48.740 --> 07:51.910
Now, representing Lady Anastasia Hoshin,

07:51.910 --> 07:55.290
I shall now relay my master's words
to you, Lady Emilia.

07:56.790 --> 07:59.960
Lady Anastasia wishes
to invite Lady Emilia

07:59.960 --> 08:02.600
to the Watergate City of Pristella.

08:03.060 --> 08:05.480
The Watergate City of Pristella?

08:05.480 --> 08:07.760
What could she want
by inviting us there?

08:08.270 --> 08:12.720
She invites you to a party
out of good will,

08:12.720 --> 08:16.520
as well as to inform you
that she has found what you are looking for.

08:17.130 --> 08:19.480
What I was looking for...?

08:19.910 --> 08:22.190
Yes, a mana crystal of the type
you desired.

08:22.190 --> 08:25.440
Apparently, it is in the hands
of a Pristellan merchant.

08:26.440 --> 08:27.780
A mana crystal...

08:28.150 --> 08:33.410
Yes. You are looking for a catalyst
to call back a Great Spirit, correct?

08:39.420 --> 08:40.790
See ya, Garf!

08:40.790 --> 08:43.250
Gonna be waiting in PriPri!

08:43.250 --> 08:45.460
Don't take too long, 'kay?

08:46.130 --> 08:49.470
She's taken quite
a liking to you, Garfiel.

08:49.470 --> 08:51.220
That doesn't make me happy at all!

08:51.220 --> 08:53.850
Oh? Your face says otherwise,
surprisingly.

08:53.850 --> 08:56.350
Quit making stuff up!

08:56.350 --> 08:57.640
You're not so honest, are you?

08:57.640 --> 08:59.310
I'm being honest-to-boot, damn it!

08:59.310 --> 09:03.440
To be honest, I'm a bit scared at the idea
of owing Anastasia a debt.

09:03.440 --> 09:05.570
Still, what kind of place is Pristella?

09:05.570 --> 09:06.950
Is it famous?

09:07.550 --> 09:10.990
Pristella is one of
the five major cities of Lugnica,

09:10.990 --> 09:14.450
located near the border
with the Kararagi city-state.

09:14.450 --> 09:19.290
They say it's a really beautiful city
with waterways running through it.

09:19.290 --> 09:22.080
A city on water, huh?

09:22.080 --> 09:25.290
Based on what I know,
it sounds like Venice or something.

09:25.290 --> 09:27.760
I've never heard of this "Venice,"

09:27.760 --> 09:30.930
but Pristella is a watergate city,
not a city on water.

09:32.090 --> 09:33.510
Meaning?

09:33.880 --> 09:37.850
The city sits in the middle of a lake,
and when it rains,

09:37.850 --> 09:39.520
the whole place gets flooded,

09:40.150 --> 09:43.440
so they built high walls around it,

09:43.440 --> 09:46.980
along with several floodgates
to control the water levels.

09:47.440 --> 09:52.700
It kinda sounds more like
a water prison now.

09:52.700 --> 09:56.450
What could she be after,
calling us to a place like that?

09:56.450 --> 10:00.660
Is it so wrong to believe she's just
reaching out to us out of goodwill?

10:00.660 --> 10:05.500
Sadly, all the royal candidates
have their own quirks.

10:08.090 --> 10:14.760
Still, I have so many things I have to talk
to Puck about, so many questions...

10:15.390 --> 10:16.390
So...

10:19.350 --> 10:22.310
You better get back to us soon,
kitty spirit!

10:22.810 --> 10:26.900
I've got a mountain of complaints
to dump on you!

10:33.320 --> 10:37.280
I'm sorry I'll be away
at such a crucial time.

10:37.800 --> 10:39.120
Oh, don't fret.

10:39.120 --> 10:44.000
I will respeeect your wishes,
even if it is a buuusy period,

10:44.000 --> 10:50.710
with all the meetings
with the western nobles.

10:52.170 --> 10:53.550
My, my.

10:53.550 --> 10:57.850
You truly haven't learned your lesson,
have you Master?

10:57.850 --> 11:00.810
Oh, you're quite harsh, Frederica.

11:00.810 --> 11:02.640
But of course.

11:02.640 --> 11:04.140
Truth be told,

11:04.140 --> 11:08.310
it would be concerning to send
Lady Emilia and Subaru alooone,

11:08.310 --> 11:12.110
but it should be fine
if Garfiel and Otto are with you.

11:12.110 --> 11:16.410
There's no need to worry about botching
the negotiations with Otto around,

11:16.410 --> 11:20.080
and worst case, Garfiel can just smash
everything and make a run for it.

11:20.620 --> 11:23.570
I feel like that'll be really problematic,

11:23.570 --> 11:26.310
so I'll do my best to make sure
it doesn't come to that!

11:26.310 --> 11:29.130
No need to worry, Emilia-tan.

11:29.130 --> 11:32.380
Whether it's Anastasia or Julius,

11:32.380 --> 11:35.970
I'm a genius at pulling wool
over people's eyes.

11:35.970 --> 11:39.600
Geez, that's not something
to be proud about!

11:39.600 --> 11:45.430
That means you'll have to stay behind
and watch the mansion alooone, Ram.

11:45.430 --> 11:48.230
Yes, if that is your wish, Lord Roswaal.

11:48.650 --> 11:50.520
The discussion is settled, then.

11:50.520 --> 11:55.530
Beatrice, look after
the four of them, would you?

11:56.580 --> 11:59.370
You don't have to
tell Betty that, I suppose!

12:03.790 --> 12:09.960
I'll have you know I'm always thinking
of what's best for everyone!

12:09.960 --> 12:13.880
Looks like you're completely
our domestic adviser now.

12:14.590 --> 12:17.130
What's that pitying look for?

12:17.130 --> 12:19.680
Calm down, Bro.

12:19.680 --> 12:23.600
And, Chief, try not to mess
with him too much, would ya?

12:23.600 --> 12:26.930
We already decided
to leave it at ten Ottos a day.

12:26.930 --> 12:31.270
What the heck
is "ten Ottos a day" anyway?!

12:49.460 --> 12:51.040
I'm coming in.

13:07.270 --> 13:08.270
Rem.

13:10.570 --> 13:13.560
Looks like we won't be seeing
each other for a while.

13:14.690 --> 13:17.650
I've got tons to talk about today.

13:18.140 --> 13:23.120
An uninvited guest dropped
one heck of a problem on us.

13:39.760 --> 13:41.630
Before we see Lady Anastasia,

13:41.630 --> 13:46.220
we should review the current state
of the royal selection.

13:46.600 --> 13:47.260
Go ahead.

13:49.350 --> 13:53.270
At first, many saw it as a contest
between Duchess Crusch Karsten,

13:53.270 --> 13:57.270
the frontrunner, and Anastasia Hoshin,
the primary challenger.

13:57.690 --> 14:00.510
Lady Emilia and the other two candidates

14:01.110 --> 14:05.590
were viewed as, frankly speaking, fillers.

14:05.590 --> 14:08.040
Yes, I don't think I can deny that.

14:08.700 --> 14:10.910
However, at the very least,

14:10.910 --> 14:13.870
public opinion has gradually
changed over the past year.

14:14.920 --> 14:17.800
Our victory over the White Whale
and the Archbishop of Sloth

14:17.800 --> 14:21.630
alongside two other major factions
played a big role in this.

14:23.120 --> 14:25.840
Aside from Lady Emilia,

14:25.840 --> 14:28.220
other factions have also made
remarkable progress,

14:28.220 --> 14:29.970
particularly Priscilla's faction.

14:30.770 --> 14:33.730
After inheriting her late
husband's domain,

14:33.730 --> 14:36.480
she quickly allied with influential figures
who were shaken

14:36.480 --> 14:38.440
by the unstable political climate.

14:39.000 --> 14:42.900
With her peerless beauty and charisma,

14:43.290 --> 14:47.370
she's now revered as the "Sun Princess,"
gaining momentum with each day.

14:47.750 --> 14:48.950
As for Felt's faction,

14:48.950 --> 14:54.500
their only advantage was the Sword Saint
Reinhard van Astrea at first.

14:55.000 --> 15:00.090
However, Lady Felt set her sights
on skilled individuals who were held back

15:00.090 --> 15:02.550
by difficult pasts or personalities,

15:02.550 --> 15:06.220
actively incorporating them to start
major reforms in her territory

15:06.220 --> 15:08.930
using her flexible thinking
and perspective.

15:09.350 --> 15:10.930
And that's how things are.

15:10.930 --> 15:14.020
No candidates have fallen off
the board this past year.

15:14.730 --> 15:15.770
It's just that...

15:17.600 --> 15:20.980
Things aren't looking good
for Duchess Crusch Karsten,

15:20.980 --> 15:25.200
as she lost her memories after her fight
with the Witch Cult.

15:25.200 --> 15:31.830
Meanwhile, Anastasia's faction
has maintained its position

15:31.830 --> 15:35.790
without decline from start to finish.

15:35.790 --> 15:42.420
Anastasia's being backed
by the massive Hoshin Company, right?

15:42.420 --> 15:46.010
Yes. Their assets are their
primary weapon.

15:46.010 --> 15:49.930
In other words, they simply crush their
opponents with sheer financial force.

15:49.930 --> 15:53.310
That invitation from Anastasia's camp
puts us in a situation

15:53.310 --> 15:55.140
where we might end up owing her.

15:55.140 --> 15:58.600
Do you understand now how much pain
you're giving my stomach?

15:58.600 --> 16:01.270
It's really sunk in now.

16:01.270 --> 16:03.360
I'm sorry for deciding things on my own.

16:03.830 --> 16:06.900
As long as you get it,
that's fine for now.

16:06.900 --> 16:10.530
You don't need to bear
everything on your own.

16:10.530 --> 16:12.330
This drake carriage is the same.

16:12.730 --> 16:14.660
This drake carriage?

16:14.660 --> 16:18.210
Mr. Natsuki is holding
its reins right now.

16:18.210 --> 16:21.920
And Beatrice is watching over him
so he doesn't slack off.

16:22.500 --> 16:28.760
Meanwhile, Garfiel is on guard duty,
and I'm planning our itinerary.

16:29.210 --> 16:31.760
Then there's you thanking everyone,

16:31.760 --> 16:37.060
motivating us to do our very best
and head for Pristella.

16:37.060 --> 16:41.270
You just sounded really
like Subaru just now.

16:41.270 --> 16:45.270
Wait, really?!
That's not very nice to hear...

16:46.690 --> 16:49.110
Hey, Otto! No fair!

16:49.110 --> 16:52.200
How come you're the only one
who gets to have fun with Emilia-tan!?

16:52.200 --> 16:55.080
- Bea-ko, take over for a bit.
- What?! Betty can't handle this alone!

16:55.080 --> 16:56.790
Stop this at once, Subaru!

16:56.790 --> 16:59.710
- Subaru!
- Hey, Chief! What're ya doin'?

16:59.710 --> 17:02.290
Is everythin' alright?!

17:02.290 --> 17:06.380
Wait, ack! Aaagh!

17:07.210 --> 17:09.930
Subaru!

17:16.890 --> 17:19.640
They're pretty strict
just for entry and exit.

17:20.200 --> 17:23.270
It's feeling more and more
like a water prison now.

17:33.570 --> 17:34.950
Wow...

17:35.990 --> 17:38.660
What a view!

17:39.200 --> 17:43.330
Pristella was originally built
on top of this lake

17:43.330 --> 17:47.050
using technology
from four hundred years ago.

17:47.480 --> 17:52.550
It's a bizarre way to build a city,
but if you think of it as one giant trap,

17:52.550 --> 17:57.470
designing it to collect water
at the center is only natural, I suppose.

17:57.470 --> 18:01.940
Calling it as one giant trap
feels really convincing.

18:01.940 --> 18:04.270
Is it a trap for some witchbeast?

18:04.270 --> 18:05.770
No one knows.

18:05.770 --> 18:09.900
I suppose there aren't any
records left for us to tell.

18:09.900 --> 18:13.360
Still, this place really
feels like a maze.

18:13.360 --> 18:17.080
The city's layout is built
around the waterways,

18:17.080 --> 18:19.830
so the land routes are all
really tangled and complex.

18:19.830 --> 18:24.080
Drake boats are also more common
than drake carriages here.

18:37.210 --> 18:39.680
The Water Raiment?

18:40.150 --> 18:43.390
This building looks
really strange, somehow.

18:43.390 --> 18:46.810
This isn't an ordinary inn.
It's a literal ryokan.

18:46.810 --> 18:49.110
Surprised, I take it?

18:49.940 --> 18:53.570
I reckon I picked the right place, then.

18:54.040 --> 18:55.450
Anastasia.

18:55.450 --> 18:58.830
Yep. Welcome to Priestella.

18:58.830 --> 19:00.990
Thanks for coming.

19:02.790 --> 19:04.580
Long time no see, Julius.

19:05.060 --> 19:07.290
Yes, it has been too long, Lady Emilia.

19:07.840 --> 19:09.590
And you as well.

19:10.120 --> 19:13.300
How have you been faring,
Sir Natsuki Subaru?

19:13.300 --> 19:16.680
Sir Subaru my ass!
You're being gross!

19:17.190 --> 19:21.520
Even so, you are a person of status now.

19:21.520 --> 19:23.560
I'm merely giving you
the respect you deserve.

19:23.940 --> 19:28.730
"The respect I deserve?" Stop it!
You're sending me chills down my spine!

19:28.730 --> 19:34.490
I see your status has had
little impact on your demeanor.

19:34.990 --> 19:39.450
I understand you're having fun
catching up, but...

19:40.490 --> 19:41.580
You are...!

19:42.700 --> 19:43.910
I am—

19:43.910 --> 19:46.120
My sincerest apologies!

19:46.570 --> 19:53.050
I never expected such an esteemed spirit
like you to grace our presence.

19:53.050 --> 19:53.880
Hmph!

19:54.760 --> 19:56.720
Fine, I'll introduce you.

19:56.720 --> 20:00.720
This is Beatrice, the loli—
I mean the spirit I've made a pact with.

20:01.160 --> 20:05.680
As Subaru's partner, it is only natural
for Betty to be here, I suppose.

20:06.220 --> 20:10.360
Do not assume Betty is the same as
those nameless lesser spirits of yours,

20:10.360 --> 20:12.820
be it in power or in cuteness.

20:12.820 --> 20:15.690
Now that you understand,

20:16.360 --> 20:19.280
you will now offer
delicious tea and sweets, I suppose.

20:19.280 --> 20:21.740
At least try to stay dignified
until the end!

20:22.780 --> 20:27.620
Garf's here! Why didn't anyone say so?

20:27.620 --> 20:30.130
Let's explore the inn together!

20:30.130 --> 20:31.920
Mimi's gonna show you the way!

20:31.920 --> 20:35.380
Hey, wait up!
I ain't agreed to anythin' yet!

20:35.380 --> 20:38.590
- She's strong!
- C'mon, let's go!

20:39.800 --> 20:41.550
We should go inside too.

20:43.010 --> 20:44.930
What happened to you?

20:44.930 --> 20:47.060
I'm fine...

20:48.070 --> 20:49.270
Completely fine...

20:50.480 --> 20:53.440
Everything here feels
really mysterious, somehow.

20:53.880 --> 20:57.650
We're sitting on the floor,
and we're not wearing shoes.

20:58.620 --> 21:03.490
The bedrooms here probably have futons
on the floor instead of beds.

21:03.990 --> 21:06.660
Are we going to wear
yukatas as loungewear?

21:06.660 --> 21:09.540
Wow, you really know
a lot about this, Subaru.

21:09.540 --> 21:11.120
Yup, you're right.

21:11.120 --> 21:14.340
Just where'd you pick up
all that Kararagi knowledge from?

21:14.340 --> 21:16.960
You mean this inn is "Kararagi" style?

21:17.380 --> 21:21.930
Yep, Japaneez-style architecture
is a Kararagi tradition.

21:22.390 --> 21:26.640
Japaneez-style...
There's no way that's a coincidence.

21:27.130 --> 21:28.730
In the first place,

21:28.730 --> 21:33.440
it was Hoshin, the hero of Kararagi,
who built Priestella.

21:33.440 --> 21:34.610
Hoshin...?

21:35.010 --> 21:37.150
Hoshin of the Wastes.

21:37.150 --> 21:39.190
He's a revolutionary from 400 years ago

21:39.190 --> 21:43.990
known for his innovative thinking
and progressive ideals.

21:44.910 --> 21:46.950
Hoshin of the Wastes, huh?

21:47.640 --> 21:50.790
He's probably the same as me,

21:50.790 --> 21:53.290
a Japanese person
transported to this world.

21:58.300 --> 22:01.470
Lady Anastasia,
the preparations are complete.

22:01.880 --> 22:03.720
Thank you, Joshua.

22:03.720 --> 22:06.680
Well then, shall we get to the main topic?

22:08.010 --> 22:11.480
The mana crystal you seek is in the hands

22:11.480 --> 22:14.650
of the heir to a major
trading company in this city.

22:15.260 --> 22:19.860
Joshua has already arranged a drake boat
bound for Muse Trading Company.

22:20.400 --> 22:22.900
Can you tell us more about this person?

22:23.370 --> 22:26.870
He's quite talented, but in this city,

22:27.520 --> 22:31.620
he's more known
by his other name.

22:31.620 --> 22:32.960
And that is...?

22:33.670 --> 22:37.710
The Man Whose Heart
Was Stolen by the Songstress.

22:38.750 --> 22:41.880
In short, the Songstress Fanatic.

22:44.090 --> 22:47.010
I've never ridden a boat on water before!

22:47.600 --> 22:49.640
I feel my heart racing, somehow.

22:49.640 --> 22:52.890
Songstress Fanatic, huh?
He's gotta be a weirdo.

22:54.020 --> 22:54.730
Hm?

22:55.600 --> 22:58.440
The water's flowing
in a different direction over there.

22:59.520 --> 23:02.990
Surprised?
Actually, I know how this works!

23:02.990 --> 23:04.570
Look!

23:04.570 --> 23:09.330
Those control towers regulate
the flow of water inside the city.

23:09.800 --> 23:13.660
I heard they're actually complex metia

23:13.660 --> 23:17.170
that use water mana crystals
to manipulate the currents.

23:17.630 --> 23:19.460
By the way,

23:19.460 --> 23:23.550
sullying the water here is a major offense,
so please be careful.

23:24.170 --> 23:28.260
Especially you, Garfiel. You've been
staring at the water like you're scared.

23:28.260 --> 23:31.140
I ain't scared of water!

23:31.140 --> 23:34.520
I just don't wanna end up like some cat
who fell down the drain!

23:34.930 --> 23:38.150
Then can you stop gripping my cloak?

23:38.680 --> 23:40.650
I think it's about to tear off.

23:41.730 --> 23:45.320
Goodness.
Everyone is so worked up.

23:45.320 --> 23:48.490
I suppose you could learn
a thing or two from Betty—

23:49.370 --> 23:50.870
Subaru?

23:52.370 --> 23:53.870
Crap...

23:54.580 --> 23:56.960
Did you just say something, I wonder?

24:00.440 --> 24:03.390
Crap... I'm about to puke...

24:06.670 --> 24:11.930
It's back... that nightmare ferry ride
on that school trip back in grade school...

24:11.930 --> 24:14.310
Crap, the world's shaking.

24:14.310 --> 24:16.560
It's still shaking...

24:16.560 --> 24:19.810
You should behave and get some
more fresh air then, I suppose.

24:19.810 --> 24:24.280
Leave the Songstress Fanatic to them.

24:24.660 --> 24:28.110
Don't tell me they knew
about my seasickness

24:28.110 --> 24:31.030
and used it to separate me
from Emilia-tan?!

24:31.030 --> 24:32.910
Emilia can handle things just fine,

24:32.910 --> 24:35.700
even if she is missing
one bumbling Subaru, I suppose.

24:35.700 --> 24:37.080
Ngh, damn it.

24:37.930 --> 24:41.500
I'm still a bit dizzy, but I can manage.

24:42.960 --> 24:46.920
I'll just hold your hand and power myself up
with heartwarming energy.

24:46.920 --> 24:48.930
You seem to be in high spirits.

24:49.430 --> 24:51.400
Well, if anything ever happens,

24:51.400 --> 24:53.430
I suppose Betty will do
something about it.

24:53.830 --> 24:55.890
Right. I'm counting on you.

24:56.310 --> 25:01.550
Okay, let's meet up with Emilia-tan
before she gets sad and lonely!

25:03.400 --> 25:06.440
Hmm, Muse Trading Company...

25:07.070 --> 25:09.780
This is the land route, right?

25:10.150 --> 25:11.530
I suppose.

25:11.980 --> 25:14.740
Uh, did we pass by it earlier?

25:16.200 --> 25:18.160
Don't tell me...

25:19.160 --> 25:20.540
...you're lost?

25:20.540 --> 25:23.750
That is not the case, I suppose!

25:23.750 --> 25:26.250
But if you're feeling anxious,

25:26.250 --> 25:29.590
it wouldn't hurt to ask someone
for directions just to be sure.

25:30.020 --> 25:32.550
Right, right. You're such a cutie.

25:33.260 --> 25:36.000
But there's no one around.

25:45.940 --> 25:54.230
♪ I wander around aimlessly... ♪

25:54.230 --> 25:55.950
♪ I wander around aimlessly... ♪
Wow.

25:56.410 --> 26:04.750
♪ No money, no future,
no dream, only vanity remains ♪

26:04.750 --> 26:06.090
No, wait.

26:06.630 --> 26:07.800
♪ Pathetic, no one's... ♪
What the heck is this?

26:07.800 --> 26:09.040
♪ Pathetic, no one's... ♪
Now that I've heard the lyrics,

26:09.040 --> 26:10.920
♪ Pathetic, no one's... ♪
this song's horrible!

26:15.470 --> 26:18.180
Crap, forgot to read the mood!

26:18.180 --> 26:20.930
Subaru, you idiot!
How can you be so rude?!

26:20.930 --> 26:23.850
- Everything is ruined!
- Nobody asked you, jackass!

26:23.850 --> 26:26.190
- Who the hell are you?
- Stop bothering us!

26:26.540 --> 26:27.610
Dumbass!

26:37.030 --> 26:39.040
That was a disaster...

26:39.040 --> 26:42.410
Honestly, that was the first time
in a year I braced myself for death.

26:42.410 --> 26:43.710
That's your problem!

26:43.710 --> 26:46.040
You'll receive no healing
from Betty, I suppose!

26:46.450 --> 26:48.500
Go ask Emilia or something.

26:48.500 --> 26:53.010
But you get upset every time
I rely on Emilia for healing.

26:54.650 --> 26:57.470
Oh, and I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to ruin—

26:57.470 --> 26:58.680
Eureka!

27:00.440 --> 27:03.270
Listen to this!
Doowawa! The Difference in Years of Love!

27:06.100 --> 27:09.110
♪ Hey, do you see it? Do you feel it? ♪

27:09.110 --> 27:12.190
♪ The difference in the years of love
between you and me! ♪

27:12.190 --> 27:18.870
♪ People call it weird, but who cares? ♪

27:18.870 --> 27:26.710
♪ Please wait a little longer,
just a little longer ♪

27:26.710 --> 27:31.960
♪ until I grow taller and reach you ♪

27:31.960 --> 27:34.670
♪ The distance of love between you and me ♪

27:34.670 --> 27:36.880
♪ A distance of love so sweet and soft— ♪

27:36.880 --> 27:39.510
♪ The gap between lovers fades from sight ♪

27:39.510 --> 27:41.970
♪ and softly ignites
into love burning bright! ♪

27:41.970 --> 27:44.230
♪ Soon the stork will pay a call ♪

27:44.230 --> 27:46.940
♪ and bless the two
with a child after all! ♪

27:46.940 --> 27:50.400
♪ It's a tale of love and bright futures! ♪

27:54.070 --> 27:55.780
What?!

27:56.170 --> 27:58.110
You must hold on a moment, I suppose!

27:58.110 --> 28:01.030
Why is Subaru suddenly
joining in the singing, I wonder?!

28:01.030 --> 28:05.160
And why are you letting him join in
like it's only natural, I wonder?!

28:05.640 --> 28:07.870
Hey, now.
What are you saying, Bea-ko?

28:07.870 --> 28:10.290
Music transcends borders, y'know?

28:10.290 --> 28:14.920
Well said! I, Liliana, am so moved
that my chest trembles in awe!

28:14.920 --> 28:16.990
Not that I have much
of a chest to tremble.

28:17.510 --> 28:21.760
It is unacceptable how you two are making
Betty the one who read the mood wrong!

28:21.760 --> 28:25.310
Whoops! I forgot to introduce myself!

28:25.730 --> 28:30.770
I'm a bard who makes a living
with nothing but my lyulyre and my voice!

28:31.230 --> 28:32.940
I'm Liliana!

28:33.610 --> 28:35.990
It's a pleasu—

28:37.240 --> 28:38.490
Bit her tongue, I suppose.

28:39.200 --> 28:40.450
Shorryh...

28:40.990 --> 28:43.160
I bit it mahgnificentlhyh...

28:44.200 --> 28:46.540
Could she be...?

28:47.120 --> 28:52.920
Hey, are you the Songstress
who's all the buzz around here?

28:52.920 --> 28:57.630
So, so... it's a pretty embarrassing nickname,
but yeah...

28:58.010 --> 29:02.740
Then you know the Songstress Fanatic
of Muse Trading Company, right?

29:04.600 --> 29:06.720
I don't mind showing you guys the way,

29:06.720 --> 29:10.810
but since you've heard
the Songstress' song, you better pay up!

29:10.810 --> 29:14.270
Didn't you say you were embarrassed
of that nickname just now?

29:14.270 --> 29:16.570
This is this, and that is that.

29:16.990 --> 29:20.570
Hey now, you're not planning
on listening for free, are you?

29:20.570 --> 29:23.030
Fine, fine! How much do you want?

29:23.030 --> 29:25.950
Just follow your heart, dear listener!

29:25.950 --> 29:27.500
Give as much as you want!

29:27.500 --> 29:29.610
Don't go forcing my heart
to do stuff for you!

29:29.610 --> 29:31.640
How could you say something like that?

29:31.640 --> 29:33.540
Eureka!

29:34.030 --> 29:37.090
Listen closely!
Rough Waves, High Tides, Society's Storms!

29:37.090 --> 29:38.800
You can stop now!

29:39.290 --> 29:42.260
And just like that,
we arrived before we knew it!

29:42.650 --> 29:44.640
So this is the place.

29:44.640 --> 29:48.810
Yes! Now please listen closely
to today's last song:

29:48.810 --> 29:50.440
Life is Full of Ups and Downs!

29:50.440 --> 29:52.850
That aside, you sure are something.

29:52.850 --> 29:57.820
I've never been this weirded out
by someone's behavior since Petelgeuse.

29:57.820 --> 30:00.320
Hoho, I don't know who that is,

30:00.320 --> 30:03.820
but this Petelgeuse seems to be quite
the remarkable individual!

30:04.370 --> 30:09.370
If we ever have the chance to meet,
he might even become my lifelong rival!

30:09.370 --> 30:11.580
He's an Archbishop of Sin.

30:14.580 --> 30:16.590
Wait, hold up a moment!

30:17.550 --> 30:19.710
Don't tell me you're...

30:19.710 --> 30:22.380
Natsuki Subaru the Kiddymancer?!

30:22.380 --> 30:25.720
I'd like to have a word or two
about that title just now...

30:26.360 --> 30:29.310
The legendary wingman
who guided Duchess Crusch Karsten's

30:29.310 --> 30:32.690
expedition against one of
the Three Great Witchbeasts, the White Whale,

30:32.690 --> 30:36.810
and placed the Sword Demon Wilhelm
in his debt!

30:36.810 --> 30:40.690
You liberated this world
from the terror of the Archbishop of Sloth

30:40.690 --> 30:43.610
with the combined forces
of Duchess Karsten

30:43.610 --> 30:45.550
and Anastasia from the Hoshin Company!

30:45.550 --> 30:46.780
And if that weren't enough,

30:46.780 --> 30:50.120
you're the hero who defeated another
Great Witchbeast, the Great Rabbit!

30:50.800 --> 30:56.540
Oh dear! Oh dear!
A living legend, right before my eyes!

30:58.460 --> 31:01.300
Miss Liliana? Is something the matter?

31:01.710 --> 31:02.920
Who are these two?

31:02.920 --> 31:07.640
Ah, we're currently here as Emilia's attendants.
She should be inside already.

31:07.640 --> 31:08.890
So that means...

31:08.890 --> 31:11.100
If I facilitate this business discussion,

31:11.100 --> 31:15.770
would the Kiddymancer Natsuki Subaru
be kind enough to tell me some things?

31:15.770 --> 31:18.230
Seriously, stop calling me that.

31:18.650 --> 31:20.480
And what do you mean by "some things"?

31:20.480 --> 31:23.320
Well, there's a lot, a whole lot!

31:23.320 --> 31:26.110
How much of the stories are true?

31:26.110 --> 31:28.950
I want to know it, hear it, sing it!

31:28.950 --> 31:33.830
I might even be able to sing an epic
that'll go down in history!

31:33.830 --> 31:35.710
Now, let's go!

31:35.710 --> 31:38.710
Smashing the scales
with obligation and sentiment

31:38.710 --> 31:40.670
is Liliana Masquerade's specialty!

31:40.670 --> 31:43.170
Just what do you mean by that, I wonder?

31:43.640 --> 31:47.680
Mr. Kiritaka is head over heels for me!

31:47.680 --> 31:48.970
So if he hears from me

31:48.970 --> 31:52.560
everything's going to be
sailing the rough seas!

31:52.560 --> 31:55.940
That doesn't sound very smooth, though!

31:55.940 --> 31:58.440
No, don't worry about it!

31:58.440 --> 32:00.020
Leave everything to me!

32:00.410 --> 32:01.900
Hey, wait up!

32:01.900 --> 32:03.530
I said wait up!

32:04.360 --> 32:08.740
Please, we would like you to hand over
that mana crystal to us.

32:10.490 --> 32:14.450
I said wait!
Come back here!

32:14.450 --> 32:17.540
Please leave everything to me!

32:17.540 --> 32:21.000
Liliana? What's happening?

32:21.630 --> 32:24.460
Please make me, Liliana, a woman!

32:25.670 --> 32:26.800
Subaru?

32:26.800 --> 32:30.300
Hey, Emilia-tan!
Fancy meeting you here!

32:30.300 --> 32:33.510
Fancy...? What are you doing here?

32:34.470 --> 32:36.520
Huh? Mr. Kiritaka?

32:37.180 --> 32:38.100
No...

32:41.190 --> 32:46.320
Stop touching my Liliana!

32:51.990 --> 32:55.370
Why in the world were you getting
touchy-feely with the Songstress

32:55.370 --> 32:58.160
in front of someone
called the Songstress Fanatic?

32:58.160 --> 33:00.420
I wasn't getting touchy-feely with her!

33:00.420 --> 33:02.790
Looked like you two
were messin' around, though.

33:02.790 --> 33:04.460
We weren't messing around!

33:04.850 --> 33:08.470
We were so close to sealing the deal,
and you just smashed it to pieces.

33:08.470 --> 33:11.340
Now now, Subaru didn't mean any harm.

33:11.340 --> 33:14.180
Emilia-tan! Go tell him more!

33:14.180 --> 33:15.850
Reflect on your actions, Subaru.

33:15.850 --> 33:18.480
Right, I'm sorry...

33:19.520 --> 33:21.310
Okay, let's leave it at that.

33:21.310 --> 33:23.770
Oh, I'm sorry!

33:23.770 --> 33:25.400
You need not be concerned.

33:25.400 --> 33:27.150
I was careless, too.

33:27.820 --> 33:30.360
After all,
you had me captivated for a moment.

33:30.950 --> 33:32.280
Huh? Er...

33:32.810 --> 33:36.160
Your beautiful silver hair, yes.

33:36.160 --> 33:37.660
Okay, hold up!

33:37.660 --> 33:39.410
That's as far as you go!

33:39.410 --> 33:45.170
You're right. Both sides were careless.
Let's leave it at that and split, alright?

33:45.580 --> 33:48.590
Subaru, that's no way
to speak to someone—

33:48.590 --> 33:50.380
Don't worry about it!

33:50.880 --> 33:53.140
Water under the bridge.

33:53.140 --> 33:56.220
A happy coincidence fit
for a water city, yeah?

33:56.220 --> 33:57.720
Thank you for your politeness.

33:58.170 --> 34:02.940
Yes, I've little reason to fixate myself
on your group for the moment.

34:03.420 --> 34:05.000
Should we ever meet again,

34:05.000 --> 34:07.900
it will simply be the whims of fate
reuniting us.

34:08.400 --> 34:13.490
Right. Here's hoping fate
makes us cross paths again, then.

34:17.740 --> 34:19.540
Something the matter, Emilia-tan?

34:19.540 --> 34:25.000
Nothing big, it's just that I feel like
I've met him before...

34:30.490 --> 34:33.880
Anyway, let's plan out our negotiations

34:33.880 --> 34:36.600
with the Songstress Fanatic
again tomorrow.

34:37.350 --> 34:40.600
I've got some matters to take care of,
so I need to head out.

34:40.600 --> 34:41.600
Matters?

34:41.600 --> 34:42.690
Yes.

34:42.690 --> 34:47.060
It's not every day we get to be in
Pristella, so I'm paying some visits.

34:48.650 --> 34:50.740
Well, someone's a hard worker.

34:50.740 --> 34:55.990
What's this?
I'm picking up a new scent at the inn.

34:56.490 --> 34:58.410
Stop makin' me repeat myself!

34:58.410 --> 35:02.250
Just shut up and bring me your boss!

35:02.250 --> 35:07.920
Someone as crude as you doesn't deserve
to see my master, not even my brother!

35:07.920 --> 35:09.480
Please leave.

35:10.610 --> 35:13.010
You just don't know
how to listen, do you, brat?!

35:13.010 --> 35:14.380
How about I just beat your ass!

35:14.380 --> 35:15.420
That's enough!

35:16.590 --> 35:17.850
Lady Emilia!

35:17.850 --> 35:19.350
You've returned!

35:19.350 --> 35:23.020
What happened?
Let's calm down and talk this over.

35:23.020 --> 35:25.140
Screw this, and everything here!

35:25.600 --> 35:28.980
This damn brat won't let me in!

35:29.430 --> 35:33.360
Wait, I've seen this guy somewhere...

35:36.530 --> 35:38.240
It's Chin!

35:38.240 --> 35:39.410
The hell's Chin?!

35:39.410 --> 35:42.620
My name is Lachins!

35:42.620 --> 35:46.150
Lachins? So you really are Chin!

35:46.150 --> 35:46.870
Screw off!

35:46.870 --> 35:49.090
Do you know him, Subaru?

35:49.090 --> 35:51.840
Yeah, from the capital.
This really takes me back.

35:52.280 --> 35:55.970
He and his friends tried to mug me.

35:56.440 --> 36:00.010
From what Betty hears,
he must be trash, I suppose.

36:00.010 --> 36:01.850
The hell are you callin' trash?!

36:01.850 --> 36:04.930
Just leave this guy to me.

36:04.930 --> 36:06.470
You son of a...

36:10.610 --> 36:13.860
I was wondering what was
taking you so long, Lachins.

36:14.690 --> 36:16.860
What's all the commotion about?

36:22.870 --> 36:24.290
Reinhard!

36:24.290 --> 36:26.870
Hi there, Subaru.
It's been too long.

36:27.290 --> 36:28.960
I've heard the stories.

36:28.960 --> 36:30.840
I'm glad you're doing well.

36:31.340 --> 36:36.300
By the way, Subaru,
I know it's been a whole year,

36:36.730 --> 36:41.140
but could you stop your friend for a bit?

36:41.570 --> 36:43.350
Calm down, Garfiel!

36:43.750 --> 36:48.350
This guy's Reinhard!
He's, uh... my friend.

36:48.350 --> 36:49.810
Don't worry about him.

36:50.480 --> 36:54.530
As he just told you,
I am Reinhard van Astrea.

36:55.030 --> 36:57.990
I would be grateful
if you told me your name.

36:59.460 --> 37:01.240
Garfiel Tinsel.

37:01.240 --> 37:05.080
I see!
So you're Lady Emilia's shield.

37:05.080 --> 37:06.250
I'm glad to meet you.

37:09.710 --> 37:11.790
I'm sorry if I offended you.

37:12.320 --> 37:13.540
I'll be careful next time.

37:15.750 --> 37:18.920
Reinhard, I'm sorry about him.

37:18.920 --> 37:20.470
Are you okay?

37:20.470 --> 37:23.350
Lady Emilia, it has been a while.

37:23.350 --> 37:28.430
Fortunately, his aim was so precise that
I could stop him without any problems.

37:28.430 --> 37:33.560
I heard from Felt that you've been
achieving really good results.

37:33.560 --> 37:37.530
Compared to your amazing exploits,
they're still very minor.

37:38.190 --> 37:43.370
Subaru, care to tell me more about
your fight with the White Whale later?

37:43.910 --> 37:47.450
That Witchbeast
isn't unrelated to me, either.

37:47.450 --> 37:51.210
Yeah, sure.
But before that...

37:51.660 --> 37:54.210
Do you know Lachins or something?

37:54.210 --> 37:58.210
Yes, he's currently
working under Lady Felt.

37:59.010 --> 38:02.180
Lachins, I'll handle the rest.

38:02.180 --> 38:05.350
Please tell Lady Felt
to return to the inn soon.

38:05.350 --> 38:06.640
Yeah, yeah.

38:07.250 --> 38:09.930
If anything happens,
please give me a signal.

38:09.930 --> 38:11.560
I'll be there in five seconds.

38:12.980 --> 38:16.120
It's scary how it sounds
like you're actually serious.

38:25.700 --> 38:29.250
Looks like he's still upset about earlier.

38:29.250 --> 38:31.330
It might be good for him once in a while.

38:31.770 --> 38:36.790
It's a good reminder that there's still
someone stronger than him, I suppose.

38:38.800 --> 38:44.010
Now, please wait here
until Lady Anastasia returns.

38:44.010 --> 38:45.550
If you'll excuse me.

38:48.010 --> 38:50.020
Oh, Subawu!

38:50.020 --> 38:51.270
Long time no see.

38:51.890 --> 38:54.480
Ferris! Ms. Crusch!

38:56.400 --> 38:57.770
And Mr. Wilhelm!

38:58.400 --> 39:00.150
Great to see you!

39:00.820 --> 39:02.240
Grandfather...

39:02.990 --> 39:05.030
Reinhard.

39:09.120 --> 39:13.460
I didn't think she'd call you here too.

39:13.860 --> 39:17.580
The same goes for us.
We didn't expect you all here.

39:17.580 --> 39:19.670
It's a fortunate coincidence.

39:19.670 --> 39:24.380
I'm surprised Mr. Wilhelm
and Reinhard were related.

39:24.880 --> 39:28.390
But they're not meeting
each other's gazes.

39:29.540 --> 39:33.810
So, why did Anastasia call you guys here?

39:33.810 --> 39:36.100
You're doubtin' us a bit too much.

39:36.100 --> 39:40.650
I really just wanted to have
a little chat, that's all.

39:40.650 --> 39:44.570
Which is why I didn't bother
invitin' the unreasonable folks.

39:45.070 --> 39:47.240
Unreasonable...?

39:47.240 --> 39:51.080
So I take it you didn't invite
Lady Priscilla, then?

39:51.550 --> 39:54.330
They do things completely
in their own way,

39:54.330 --> 39:57.500
so I couldn't think of
an excuse to call them over.

39:57.990 --> 40:01.170
Well, at least Felt and I
are a bit closer now.

40:01.830 --> 40:03.260
An excuse?

40:03.260 --> 40:05.380
If you all were comin' anyway,

40:05.380 --> 40:08.340
I thought I'd at least
prepare a lil' gift.

40:08.970 --> 40:12.390
Then for Ms. Crusch, that would be...

40:13.800 --> 40:16.890
We came here
because Lady Anastasia claimed

40:17.350 --> 40:23.150
to have information
regarding the Archbishop of Gluttony.

40:25.650 --> 40:29.070
Now, don't get me wrong here, Natsuki.

40:29.700 --> 40:36.500
It's just that Ms. Crusch here
is the better buyer.

40:37.410 --> 40:40.250
A merchant through and through, huh?

40:40.250 --> 40:42.670
Ticks me off, but I understand your logic.

40:43.130 --> 40:45.380
It seems you're more mature now.

40:45.380 --> 40:49.510
Shut it! Don't tempt me
when I'm barely holding it in!

40:49.510 --> 40:51.680
Now, don't go makin' that face now.

40:51.680 --> 40:54.470
I'm not goin' to hide it from you.

40:54.970 --> 40:57.230
Ms. Crusch here doesn't
want to leave you out.

40:57.680 --> 41:00.310
She's a goody-two-shoes
through and through.

41:01.400 --> 41:04.270
Naturally, I wish to settle things
with Gluttony myself,

41:04.770 --> 41:08.030
as it concerns my memories.

41:08.030 --> 41:13.240
However, I am also aware that it is
your fondest wish to help Rem.

41:13.660 --> 41:15.040
Ms. Crusch...

41:15.040 --> 41:19.580
Besides, I believe it would be better
to have more people united to our cause.

41:20.500 --> 41:24.290
Let's not hold grudges
on whoever's blade reaches him first.

41:25.000 --> 41:30.010
Really, thank you.
I'll definitely answer your expectations.

41:30.470 --> 41:32.720
I swear it.

41:33.400 --> 41:36.810
Even so, we will likely reach him first.

41:38.000 --> 41:40.940
Oh? Looks like everyone's here!

41:40.940 --> 41:44.520
It's surprising how little you've all
changed despite a whole year passing by!

41:45.020 --> 41:47.780
Well, the same goes for me, I guess.

41:47.780 --> 41:48.780
Lady Felt!

41:49.350 --> 41:54.450
What happened to the attire
you were given to wear in public?

41:54.450 --> 41:58.000
Ha! You expect me
to go along with your taste?

41:58.560 --> 42:03.630
Sightseeing was the perfect excuse
to find myself some proper clothes!

42:03.630 --> 42:05.920
Truly, you are so...

42:09.380 --> 42:13.010
I am truly grateful for the invitation.

42:13.720 --> 42:19.220
Now, let us have a fruitful discussion
as fellow candidates.

42:20.270 --> 42:22.190
Okay, formalities over!

42:22.600 --> 42:24.400
Let me in the talks, yeah?

42:24.820 --> 42:28.320
I have to say, this is a weird city.
This building's weird too.

42:28.320 --> 42:31.240
Seeing all this unusual stuff
everywhere is wearing me out!

42:31.240 --> 42:33.910
You never cease to amaze.

42:33.910 --> 42:35.910
Unusual, you say?

42:35.910 --> 42:38.700
If you think of it that way,
then I'm happy.

42:39.870 --> 42:43.170
This ryokan's still got
plenty more to offer.

42:43.560 --> 42:48.000
Ah, this is heaven!

42:48.000 --> 42:48.950
Chief.

42:49.920 --> 42:50.970
What's up?

42:51.510 --> 42:56.140
Sorry, but do ya mind
if I head out for a bit?

42:59.140 --> 43:00.600
Don't worry, Garfiel.

43:00.600 --> 43:03.060
You're plenty strong.

43:03.520 --> 43:05.770
But not the strongest.

43:06.360 --> 43:09.070
That ain't good enough.

43:11.360 --> 43:14.780
He'll get back to his feet
after a good night's rest.

43:15.200 --> 43:16.390
Peek...

43:17.820 --> 43:18.910
Peek peek...

43:19.490 --> 43:22.790
Sneak sneak...

43:23.400 --> 43:24.670
Sneak sneak...

43:24.670 --> 43:27.500
How is it, I wonder?

43:30.840 --> 43:31.760
Bea-ko!

43:31.760 --> 43:34.510
What's with that getup?!

43:34.510 --> 43:39.510
Today's Betty
is a different flavor than usual!

43:39.510 --> 43:42.100
Amazing! They even got yukatas here?!

43:42.100 --> 43:45.850
Bea-ko, you're so pretty!
Bea-ko, you're so lovely!

43:45.850 --> 43:48.110
Don't get too carried away, Subaru.

43:48.110 --> 43:51.650
Emilia...taaaan?!

43:57.490 --> 43:58.490
Subaru?

43:59.050 --> 44:01.450
You're breathing heavily
through your nose.

44:01.450 --> 44:02.700
Do you have a fever?

44:02.700 --> 44:05.040
A slight fever of love, maybe...

44:05.040 --> 44:06.000
Hey!

44:06.000 --> 44:07.710
They told me in the bath.

44:07.710 --> 44:12.170
I heard my garbage knight
bullied your blonde boy?

44:12.170 --> 44:16.090
Lady Felt,
we merely had a misunderstanding.

44:16.090 --> 44:20.300
He's actually tremendously powerful
despite his young age.

44:20.300 --> 44:24.220
That patronizing lack of self-awareness
really isn't convincing...

44:24.600 --> 44:30.690
By the way, Lady Felt,
those clothes suit you well.

44:30.690 --> 44:31.820
Shaddap.

44:32.250 --> 44:37.450
Man, you're really rough
on Reinhard, aren't you?

44:37.900 --> 44:40.450
Well, I started with ulterior motives,

44:41.100 --> 44:46.370
so I guess Crusch and Ferris
have the most ideal relationship.

44:47.500 --> 44:51.080
Hearing you say that makes me blush.

44:51.080 --> 44:52.880
Right, Ferris?

44:52.880 --> 44:57.380
Well, I definitely have
ulterior motives for you, Lady Crusch.

45:00.300 --> 45:02.680
Okay, we should eat now.

45:02.680 --> 45:04.350
M-Master Subaru!

45:04.350 --> 45:07.180
Please don't run away
while leaving the mood like that!

45:07.180 --> 45:11.810
Don't worry,
we were just joking awound!

45:14.480 --> 45:16.480
You really are spineless.

45:18.820 --> 45:23.580
You already know
why you keep seeing me, right?

45:23.580 --> 45:24.620
Shut up!

45:25.200 --> 45:27.790
Shut your mouth!

45:30.120 --> 45:33.090
That's right.
You are weak.

45:33.960 --> 45:39.340
The only reason you didn't get killed
by me was simply pure luck.

45:39.930 --> 45:44.350
And the reason you were able
to kill me was pure coincidence.

45:44.740 --> 45:46.310
Shut up!

45:46.310 --> 45:48.850
You're weak, after all.

45:49.560 --> 45:52.350
You're nothing more than
a spineless weakling...

45:53.770 --> 45:55.570
...yet you still murdered me.

46:01.150 --> 46:03.700
Oh, it's Garf!

46:04.200 --> 46:05.990
Where are ya headed to?

46:05.990 --> 46:08.200
Mimi's coming too!

46:10.210 --> 46:13.580
Hm? You're making a weird face, Garf!

46:14.020 --> 46:16.340
Did something interesting happen?

46:16.340 --> 46:19.760
Does it look like
I'm in a good mood, genius?

46:19.760 --> 46:22.590
I don't wanna talk,
and I don't have a reason to.

46:22.590 --> 46:25.680
Keep talking about things
like "loyaltie" and "dooty,"

46:25.680 --> 46:27.470
and you'll end up like Joshua!

46:29.020 --> 46:31.640
Mimi thinks it's better to relax
and go with the flow.

46:32.560 --> 46:36.940
Garf looks cooler laughing like an idiot!

46:39.030 --> 46:41.780
The hell are ya callin' an idiot?!

46:49.160 --> 46:51.620
Garf! Look, look!

46:51.620 --> 46:53.800
The sunset's so pretty!

46:53.800 --> 46:55.420
It's so red!

46:56.080 --> 46:58.420
Hey, calm down for a sec, would ya?!

46:59.130 --> 47:00.210
Nah!

47:00.210 --> 47:02.050
No hesitation, huh?

47:09.310 --> 47:13.060
Well, no use moping around about it.

47:13.060 --> 47:14.640
What's up?

47:14.640 --> 47:15.940
It's nothin'.

47:16.360 --> 47:19.400
Just realized I can't become
the strongest outta nowhere.

47:19.830 --> 47:23.110
I'm still in the middle
of climbin' my way up!

47:23.110 --> 47:27.950
Right! Sounds like
a really really tall climb!

47:27.950 --> 47:31.410
Oh? Looks like you're gettin' it!

47:31.410 --> 47:32.410
That's right!

47:32.410 --> 47:36.100
That's the road to being the strongest!

47:38.590 --> 47:40.420
Garf! Look!

47:57.810 --> 47:59.940
There we go.

47:59.940 --> 48:01.650
Wow!

48:02.070 --> 48:03.610
So kewl!

48:03.610 --> 48:08.320
M-Mister! Thank you very much!

48:08.320 --> 48:10.530
Don't worry about it!

48:11.030 --> 48:13.790
What's your name, Mister?

48:13.790 --> 48:16.000
Nothin' worth mentionin'!

48:16.540 --> 48:20.040
But if ya gotta call me somethin',
then call me Tiger...

48:20.040 --> 48:23.630
Gorgeous Tiger!

48:24.040 --> 48:26.630
Gorgeous... Tiger!

48:27.070 --> 48:29.090
Gorgeous Tiger!

48:29.470 --> 48:31.810
You're so cool!

48:33.560 --> 48:35.180
Gorgeous!

48:35.180 --> 48:37.480
Can we eat these as-is?

48:37.970 --> 48:39.600
Never seen it before, have you?

48:39.600 --> 48:45.070
You can't make these without
bein' near the Great Tigrasea River.

48:46.320 --> 48:49.260
And this is how you eat it!

48:50.990 --> 48:53.740
Delicious!
It's been ages since I've had sashimi!

48:53.740 --> 48:57.460
You're the best, Anastasia!
The very best!

48:57.460 --> 48:59.250
I-It's tasty?

48:59.250 --> 49:00.710
It's absolutely delicious!

49:00.710 --> 49:04.210
It's fresh too, so it's really tasty!

49:06.210 --> 49:08.090
What's wrong, Bea-ko?

49:08.090 --> 49:11.390
I-Is this green clump poison, I wonder?!

49:11.930 --> 49:16.560
Betty's nose is going ziiing! Ziiing!

49:17.480 --> 49:20.810
And that was when I told 'em:

49:20.810 --> 49:25.400
I've seen through
your evil deeds, small fries!

49:25.400 --> 49:27.690
So kewl! Gives goosebumps!

49:28.110 --> 49:29.770
Wow!

49:30.530 --> 49:33.950
- So, is your house around here?
- Yes!

49:34.490 --> 49:38.710
Ya little kids sure came a long way.

49:38.710 --> 49:42.630
I wonder if Sis is mad at me.
I didn't tell her I was going out.

49:42.630 --> 49:47.340
Got a scary sis?
I know the feeling.

49:47.340 --> 49:50.010
Alright! Leave everythin' to me!

49:50.010 --> 49:52.340
Really, Gorgeous Tiger?

49:52.340 --> 49:53.390
Fred!

49:53.770 --> 49:56.100
- S-Sis...
- What are you doing?!

49:56.530 --> 49:59.310
Just how much were you
trying to make us worry?!

49:59.310 --> 50:02.770
C'mon, Sis.
This guy didn't mean any harm.

50:03.170 --> 50:05.480
- Can't you cut him some...
- Dear?

50:06.620 --> 50:08.320
Did you find Fred?

50:10.570 --> 50:13.490
It looks like you were
taking care of my children.

50:14.370 --> 50:15.830
I'm sorry for the trouble.

50:34.650 --> 50:36.260
Mom...?

50:40.560 --> 50:43.030
Can't eat anymore...

50:44.630 --> 50:49.940
But I suppose this ziiing
might not be so bad after all...

50:58.080 --> 51:00.370
Did I startle you?

51:00.370 --> 51:03.040
Nah, you just had me
captivated for a second.

51:03.410 --> 51:06.250
The Sword Demon in a Japanese garden.
It's such a perfect match.

51:06.250 --> 51:09.000
I have a soft spot for people
who shine in the moonlight.

51:09.000 --> 51:14.340
You should whisper those words
to a woman, not to me.

51:14.340 --> 51:15.970
What a waste.

51:15.970 --> 51:19.600
Right now, this kind of flowery talk

51:19.600 --> 51:22.680
doesn't work on the girl whose heart
I want to tickle the most.

51:22.680 --> 51:26.060
That frustration is yet another part
of the joys of love.

51:26.600 --> 51:29.900
In the mood for some
nostalgic love stories, I see.

51:29.900 --> 51:31.610
Care to listen?

51:31.610 --> 51:32.650
Of course.

51:34.280 --> 51:35.280
Well then...

51:37.270 --> 51:40.990
My past self was clumsy with words,
far worse than I am right now.

51:40.990 --> 51:43.710
A man lacking in words.

51:44.580 --> 51:48.330
The sword was everything to me.

51:49.590 --> 51:52.130
The thoughts stirring within me
before each strike

51:52.130 --> 51:54.670
and the thoughts born with every swing

51:55.220 --> 51:58.050
were what shaped my entirety.

51:58.050 --> 52:02.720
It was my wife who made me realize
such a simple truth.

52:03.180 --> 52:07.350
And so, every time I held my sword,
I would remember her.

52:07.350 --> 52:09.150
Even now?

52:10.780 --> 52:13.400
Be it then or now,

52:13.400 --> 52:15.900
the sword has always linked me to my wife.

52:17.160 --> 52:21.930
As long as I held the sword, my feelings
for my wife would undoubtedly persist.

52:23.160 --> 52:26.660
Your missus was
the previous Sword Saint, right?

52:27.080 --> 52:28.630
In times of peace,

52:28.630 --> 52:32.630
she was an ordinary woman
who loved flowers.

52:33.380 --> 52:36.010
The heroes who left their mark on history

52:36.010 --> 52:39.890
did not necessarily continue
being heroes in their daily lives.

52:39.890 --> 52:43.350
You are no different, Sir Subaru.

52:43.870 --> 52:48.190
Your name has spread
further than you think.

52:48.670 --> 52:50.190
I don't think...

52:50.190 --> 52:52.150
I am certain of it.

52:52.810 --> 52:55.530
For anything you cannot accomplish,

52:55.530 --> 53:00.160
you gather others who cannot accomplish
the same and make it possible.

53:00.560 --> 53:04.490
I'm just a weakling
who can't do anything.

53:04.490 --> 53:10.630
Yes, and it is that very weakling
who can't do anything whom I like.

53:12.560 --> 53:15.000
It seems I've rambled too much.

53:16.300 --> 53:21.510
I have to say, every time
I speak with you, I always think...

53:23.400 --> 53:30.230
Why am I incapable of speaking
to my own grandson?

53:30.880 --> 53:33.610
You don't get along with Reinhard?

53:34.110 --> 53:35.190
Aren't you family?

53:37.280 --> 53:39.900
Over the course of my life,

53:39.900 --> 53:43.410
I have three regrets of which
I have no excuses for.

53:45.990 --> 53:52.330
One of which is the cause of the rift
between my grandson and I.

53:54.840 --> 53:59.550
I was so foolish,
so unforgivably foolish.

54:00.510 --> 54:05.890
I used the hunt for my wife's killer
as an excuse to flee from my regrets.

54:06.340 --> 54:08.770
And now that I have avenged her,

54:08.770 --> 54:12.350
I understand that now
is truly the time to approach him.

54:13.400 --> 54:15.690
But you're too scared...

54:16.200 --> 54:18.530
As ashamed as I am.

54:24.780 --> 54:29.120
Reinhard told me he wanted to hear more
about the battle with the White Whale.

54:30.830 --> 54:35.170
I don't know what the White Whale
has to do with you two not getting along,

54:35.650 --> 54:41.880
but Reinhard knows you spent
over a decade to avenge his grandma.

54:42.630 --> 54:44.680
He wants to hear more about it.

54:45.990 --> 54:48.640
I'm sure he's looking forward to it,

54:49.390 --> 54:52.060
to you bringing it up to him.

54:54.960 --> 54:56.470
Unbelievable.

54:57.940 --> 55:00.990
It seems there is no besting you,
Sir Subaru.

55:11.790 --> 55:22.220
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight!

55:22.720 --> 55:25.300
Now, raise both your arms, and...

55:25.300 --> 55:27.640
Victory!

55:28.310 --> 55:31.560
You're in a really good mood
this morning, Subaru!

55:31.560 --> 55:34.230
I just had a chat
before sleeping last night.

55:34.230 --> 55:36.440
Is that so? That's nice.

55:36.900 --> 55:39.520
You looked like you had
something in your mind.

55:40.650 --> 55:44.070
Unlike Subaru,
his morning is not so pleasant, though.

55:47.840 --> 55:49.910
Got a hangover, Otto?

55:49.910 --> 55:53.160
Y-Yes... It's not every day
I can go to Pristella,

55:53.160 --> 55:56.290
so I had to go drinking
and make connectio—

55:56.290 --> 55:57.290
Watch out!

55:57.290 --> 56:00.250
By the way, I don't see Garfiel anywhere.

56:01.880 --> 56:03.090
He's a bit...

56:03.590 --> 56:05.760
...sensitive right now.

56:05.760 --> 56:08.300
Be nice to him when he gets back, okay?

56:09.600 --> 56:13.140
So, Otto-kun, what's the plan for today?

56:13.140 --> 56:16.020
I think you were planning
to take Liliana as a hostage

56:16.020 --> 56:18.350
and trade her for that mana crystal?

56:18.350 --> 56:21.320
For now, let's leave Mr. Natsuki behind...

56:21.320 --> 56:22.900
I won't accept any objections...

56:23.860 --> 56:25.820
Yo! You're all together!

56:25.820 --> 56:28.280
And up early, too.

56:28.650 --> 56:32.290
Hm? I didn't see this green guy yesterday.

56:32.290 --> 56:37.290
He's our domestic adviser,
more or less our equivalent of Chin.

56:37.290 --> 56:41.040
Come to think of it,
isn't Reinhard accompanying you?

56:41.040 --> 56:45.090
I ain't a kid, and he's just
gonna pester me all day.

56:45.090 --> 56:49.340
Besides, I hate to admit it,
but if I call for him,

56:49.340 --> 56:51.510
he'll be here in a second.

56:51.510 --> 56:53.350
Did you call for me, Lady Felt?

56:53.350 --> 56:54.810
I did not!

56:54.810 --> 56:58.470
Good morning, Lady Emilia, Subaru.

56:58.470 --> 56:59.650
Nice morning, isn't it?

57:01.210 --> 57:04.150
You two really get along, don't you.

57:04.150 --> 57:08.200
Yeah, you two're the very picture
of getting along.

57:09.280 --> 57:14.200
You guys are making my skin crawl!

57:26.220 --> 57:31.180
Good mornin'. Looks like you're all
gettin' along rather nicely.

57:31.180 --> 57:32.470
Lady Anastasia.

57:33.560 --> 57:35.470
Your beauty grows with each morning.

57:37.140 --> 57:39.270
It's one of my secret tricks.

57:39.820 --> 57:43.270
Oh? Mimi and Rickard aren't with you?

57:43.670 --> 57:45.400
Rickard has yet to return.

57:45.400 --> 57:47.510
And about Mimi...

57:48.070 --> 57:50.610
She seems to have gone out with Garfiel.

57:51.210 --> 57:53.570
Hetaro and Tibby rushed out of the inn

57:53.570 --> 57:57.080
when they heard Mimi
didn't return last night.

57:57.080 --> 58:01.330
Hetaro gets tunnel vision
when Mimi is involved.

58:01.760 --> 58:04.210
But he should be fine
as long as Tibby's with him.

58:04.890 --> 58:08.420
That's why I'm going to
ask you instead, Joshua.

58:08.420 --> 58:09.970
Wh-What is it?

58:10.460 --> 58:15.350
I want you to pick up a letter
at the main gate,

58:15.350 --> 58:19.130
a very, very important letter.

58:19.130 --> 58:20.940
Is it related to Gluttony?!

58:21.370 --> 58:24.190
I'm begging you, Joshua!
You're my only hope!

58:24.190 --> 58:27.010
Why do you need to tell me th...

58:30.030 --> 58:31.570
Apologies for the delay.

58:32.010 --> 58:34.070
It seems we're the last to arrive.

58:34.660 --> 58:37.030
Looks like we're all here for breakfast.

58:37.030 --> 58:39.540
Okay, bring it in!

58:45.630 --> 58:47.250
Wait, I know this!

58:47.800 --> 58:52.090
Today's breakfast
is Kararagi-style traditional cuisine:

58:52.800 --> 58:54.390
Daisukiyaki!

58:54.390 --> 58:57.600
O-Okonomiyaki?!

59:03.690 --> 59:04.810
Look, Subaru!

59:04.810 --> 59:08.650
Look at how prettily I flipped it over!
I'm so proud of this! Eat up!

59:08.650 --> 59:11.320
So-so, I suppose.

59:11.320 --> 59:17.830
Subaru, you may eat the daisukiyaki
Betty so graciously made for you.

59:18.410 --> 59:20.040
Beatrice...

59:20.040 --> 59:22.000
That's way too much sauce!

59:22.000 --> 59:23.120
You too, Lady Emilia!

59:23.120 --> 59:25.370
Frying it too lightly
will ruin your stomach!

59:25.370 --> 59:30.550
You two should try tasting your own food
before serving it to others...

59:32.760 --> 59:34.880
Lady Felt, this batch is done.

59:34.880 --> 59:39.300
Yeah, sure, keep up the good work.

59:44.940 --> 59:48.310
I think I just saw something
I shouldn't have...

59:48.310 --> 59:51.690
Good morning, citizens of Pristella!

59:51.690 --> 59:53.070
- It's quite a beautiful morning, isn't it?

59:53.070 --> 59:53.900
- Huh? What the heck is this?
- It's quite a beautiful morning, isn't it?

59:53.900 --> 59:55.280
- Huh? What the heck is this?
- This morning's first cup features

59:55.280 --> 59:57.780
- It's a morning staple here,
- premium tea direct from Kararagi,

59:57.780 --> 59:58.930
- a metropolitan-government broadcast
- accompanied by

59:58.930 --> 01:00:00.830
- using a metia.
- a slice of three-year-old bambeem.

01:00:00.830 --> 01:00:03.290
- A metia broadcast...?
- Its delightful aroma fills the air,

01:00:03.290 --> 01:00:04.540
- Its delightful aroma fills the air,

01:00:04.540 --> 01:00:05.120
- So there's a broadcast every day?
- Its delightful aroma fills the air,

01:00:05.120 --> 01:00:06.830
- So there's a broadcast every day?
- mingling with the vibrant

01:00:06.830 --> 01:00:08.630
- What for?
- and refreshing scent of the premium tea

01:00:08.630 --> 01:00:11.050
- I heard it is to prepare for emergencies,
- as sunlight pours in through the window.

01:00:11.050 --> 01:00:12.840
- as the structure of this city
- It seems like today is going to be

01:00:12.840 --> 01:00:14.010
- allows for few evacuation routes.
- another wonderful day.

01:00:14.010 --> 01:00:15.470
- allows for few evacuation routes.
- Now, I'd like to offer everyone

01:00:15.470 --> 01:00:17.680
- Oh? Makes swense.
- a little something from my heart...

01:00:18.060 --> 01:00:21.890
- Incidentally, Mr. Kiritaka is the broadcaster
- or rather, a wonderful blessing!

01:00:21.890 --> 01:00:23.390
- and provider of the metia.
- It's time for the Songstress,

01:00:23.390 --> 01:00:24.450
- Miss Liliana Masquerade,

01:00:24.450 --> 01:00:26.020
- Yep, that's definitely him.
- to take the stageeeeee!

01:00:26.520 --> 01:00:29.150
Hey there, everyone! Liliana here!

01:00:29.640 --> 01:00:33.400
I'm gonna sing and play my heart out
to bring you joy,

01:00:33.400 --> 01:00:38.160
so I hope you all have fun
during our brief time together!

01:00:38.160 --> 01:00:39.570
Cheer me on, okay?

01:00:41.280 --> 01:00:43.870
Now, without further ado,
please listen to...

01:00:44.310 --> 01:00:46.290
The Love Song of the Sword Demon, Act 2!

01:00:46.830 --> 01:00:48.090
Stu...

01:00:51.500 --> 01:01:01.100
♪ In the outskirts of town,
in a quiet, empty corner ♪

01:01:01.100 --> 01:01:10.600
♪ The Sword Demon wanders,
solitude in hand ♪

01:01:10.600 --> 01:01:15.530
♪ But what awaits him is a field of flowers ♪

01:01:15.530 --> 01:01:20.280
♪ "Hey, do you like flowers?" ♪

01:01:20.280 --> 01:01:21.950
Reinhard.

01:01:23.450 --> 01:01:25.790
Well, you see...!

01:01:25.790 --> 01:01:27.460
Yes, what is it?

01:01:28.000 --> 01:01:30.920
I... cannot... fry it properly...!

01:01:31.460 --> 01:01:34.880
I-If you have any tips...
could you... perhaps tell me?

01:01:39.680 --> 01:01:42.600
Yes. I understand, Grandfather.

01:01:52.650 --> 01:01:54.360
Nope, not happening.

01:01:54.790 --> 01:01:58.000
Ain't it too convenient for you
to pull that out this late in the game?

01:02:01.180 --> 01:02:02.530
My honored Father?

01:02:08.410 --> 01:02:10.250
Who the hell are you?

01:02:11.210 --> 01:02:12.460
Hah?

01:02:12.950 --> 01:02:17.170
Those're some nasty eyes you've got, brat.

01:02:21.010 --> 01:02:25.890
Hey, I don't care
if it's the Sword Saint or Juukulius,

01:02:25.890 --> 01:02:27.350
someone kill this rude brat.

01:02:27.890 --> 01:02:32.310
With all due respect,
both Reinhard and I are on special duty,

01:02:32.310 --> 01:02:34.440
meaning we're not under
our usual obligations.

01:02:34.990 --> 01:02:36.730
Even if you are the vice captain,

01:02:36.730 --> 01:02:39.650
I believe you don't have
the authority to give us orders.

01:02:39.650 --> 01:02:43.990
Hey now, don't give me that scary face!
I was obviously kidding!

01:02:43.990 --> 01:02:45.700
Calm down.

01:02:45.700 --> 01:02:51.330
Even if I am vice captain in name only,
I follow the rules.

01:02:51.330 --> 01:02:53.370
In name?

01:02:53.370 --> 01:02:55.420
Right. I'm just a figurehead.

01:02:55.420 --> 01:03:00.340
I'm none other than the hated
ornamental vice captain,

01:03:00.340 --> 01:03:03.680
"Heinkel the Idle" in the flesh.

01:03:03.680 --> 01:03:07.560
Stop boasting about
being hated and idle.

01:03:07.560 --> 01:03:09.390
Calm down, Subaru.

01:03:09.390 --> 01:03:11.770
You mustn't get caught
in his rhythm.

01:03:11.770 --> 01:03:14.150
Ha! The "Finest" indeed.

01:03:14.150 --> 01:03:16.230
Such a well-mannered choice of words.

01:03:16.230 --> 01:03:17.610
Heinkel!

01:03:20.340 --> 01:03:21.860
Heinkel...!

01:03:21.860 --> 01:03:24.410
I heard you the first time.

01:03:24.410 --> 01:03:27.410
I'm not that old yet.
I can still hear.

01:03:27.410 --> 01:03:30.040
Anyway, you guys are so cold,

01:03:30.040 --> 01:03:35.510
leaving me out of the White Whale
hunt celebration like that!

01:03:36.000 --> 01:03:38.460
Ain't that right, my honored Father?

01:03:38.460 --> 01:03:41.050
Heinkel... I...

01:03:41.590 --> 01:03:42.920
Reinhard!

01:03:43.320 --> 01:03:44.840
You feel the same way, don't you?

01:03:45.630 --> 01:03:49.760
Father lifted a burden
on your shoulders, yeah?

01:03:50.810 --> 01:03:57.610
He did avenge your predecessor,
the very same woman you got killed.

01:03:57.610 --> 01:03:59.320
Enough, Heinkel!

01:03:59.670 --> 01:04:00.900
You...

01:04:00.900 --> 01:04:03.070
Even for you, this is...!

01:04:03.070 --> 01:04:04.530
How much must you...!

01:04:04.530 --> 01:04:08.280
It's too late to pretty things up, Father.

01:04:08.280 --> 01:04:11.490
You of all people don't have
the right to criticize me.

01:04:11.990 --> 01:04:15.460
We all know the first to blame Reinhard
for killing his predecessor

01:04:15.460 --> 01:04:18.330
was none other than you.

01:04:21.030 --> 01:04:23.760
Going quiet the moment the truth
gets inconvenient for you?

01:04:23.760 --> 01:04:26.260
You think you can patch
things up with that?

01:04:26.260 --> 01:04:27.930
That's too convenient.

01:04:27.930 --> 01:04:31.510
Theresia van Astrea would never
accept something like that.

01:04:31.940 --> 01:04:34.480
Heinkel van Astrea!

01:04:35.310 --> 01:04:37.100
Don't add the "van" in, brat!

01:04:37.560 --> 01:04:39.100
I never got the sword name.

01:04:39.100 --> 01:04:41.320
I'm just plain ol' Heinkel Astrea.

01:04:41.970 --> 01:04:45.150
So, why have you come here?

01:04:45.560 --> 01:04:46.610
Emilia...

01:04:46.610 --> 01:04:48.070
Well well!

01:04:48.070 --> 01:04:50.120
So you're Lady Emilia!

01:04:50.120 --> 01:04:55.660
The half-witch princess
who's fighting a battle she can't win-

01:04:55.660 --> 01:05:00.210
We're not talking about
your opinion of me right now.

01:05:00.720 --> 01:05:02.840
I only have one question.

01:05:02.840 --> 01:05:05.170
Why have you come here?

01:05:06.170 --> 01:05:09.180
Tch, this ain't what the rumors said...

01:05:09.580 --> 01:05:10.890
Answer properly.

01:05:13.470 --> 01:05:18.850
So, you're clamming up
after barging in all smug? Pathetic.

01:05:18.850 --> 01:05:22.980
And here I was expecting
something entertaining.

01:05:22.980 --> 01:05:26.440
Uncouth individuals
should make themselves scarce.

01:05:26.440 --> 01:05:29.200
Are you satisfied, Vice Captain?

01:05:29.200 --> 01:05:31.280
If you have no further business,

01:05:31.280 --> 01:05:34.490
it would be to our mutual benefit
for you to depart at once.

01:05:36.700 --> 01:05:39.290
That will not be necessary, commoner.

01:05:39.290 --> 01:05:40.830
What took you so long?!

01:05:40.830 --> 01:05:44.800
I was sweating buckets here
waiting for you, Miss Priscilla!

01:05:45.570 --> 01:05:46.760
Silence.

01:05:47.720 --> 01:05:49.430
Ah, yes, what a nostalgic lineup.

01:05:49.850 --> 01:05:51.930
I see you're all getting along, hm?

01:05:52.330 --> 01:05:55.510
Priscilla! Did you bring him here?!

01:05:59.440 --> 01:06:00.560
And who might you be?

01:06:00.560 --> 01:06:02.310
You don't remember me?!

01:06:02.310 --> 01:06:05.690
C'mon, Princess,
that's too cruel even for you.

01:06:05.690 --> 01:06:07.530
Remember that guy who shamed himself

01:06:07.530 --> 01:06:10.640
in front of everyone during
the declaration of beliefs at the castle?

01:06:10.640 --> 01:06:12.410
That's this bro right there.

01:06:12.410 --> 01:06:15.200
You were grabbing your belly
laughing at him, remember?

01:06:15.200 --> 01:06:16.580
I've no memory of it.

01:06:16.580 --> 01:06:19.290
And do I look like
I'd debase myself in crude acts

01:06:19.290 --> 01:06:21.460
such as grabbing my belly while laughing?

01:06:21.460 --> 01:06:23.420
Do not spin fairytales now, Al.

01:06:23.420 --> 01:06:25.000
You heard her, bro.

01:06:25.000 --> 01:06:26.590
Sorry I couldn't do more.

01:06:26.590 --> 01:06:30.300
It's been a year man! Couldn't you
get better at talking at least?!

01:06:30.300 --> 01:06:33.180
Good luck, bro.
You'll have to butter her up from scratch.

01:06:35.100 --> 01:06:36.930
So, care to answer my question?

01:06:36.930 --> 01:06:40.890
You are asking whether
I brought this commoner here?

01:06:40.890 --> 01:06:43.150
In that case, you are correct.

01:06:43.150 --> 01:06:47.610
I called him here and brought him with me.

01:06:48.530 --> 01:06:49.690
But why?

01:06:50.360 --> 01:06:51.990
If I must provide a reason,

01:06:52.610 --> 01:06:55.410
it is simply that it offers
more amusement.

01:06:56.370 --> 01:07:00.580
An awkward attempt
to rectify warped family bonds!

01:07:00.580 --> 01:07:05.250
I cannot possibly stand idly by and allow
such a pathetic performance to unfold now.

01:07:05.250 --> 01:07:07.840
As such, I have decided
to rewrite the script.

01:07:07.840 --> 01:07:09.420
It was quite amusing, was it not?

01:07:09.420 --> 01:07:10.670
Priscilla!

01:07:10.670 --> 01:07:12.380
Hold up, bro.

01:07:12.380 --> 01:07:14.430
No one's getting anything
out of fighting here.

01:07:14.430 --> 01:07:16.300
Cut the crap!

01:07:16.300 --> 01:07:20.770
You're telling me it's okay to emotionally
abuse people all you want?!

01:07:20.770 --> 01:07:22.230
Subaru...

01:07:29.890 --> 01:07:33.860
I don't remember invitin' you
out of all people.

01:07:34.330 --> 01:07:38.120
Sly fox, when a word finds its way
into the ears of men,

01:07:38.120 --> 01:07:40.990
it is inevitable that it
shall flow forth like tears.

01:07:40.990 --> 01:07:44.500
This old guy is Reinhard's dad, right?

01:07:44.500 --> 01:07:50.750
Oh? Does the gutter rat
dare to offer me her opinions?

01:07:51.150 --> 01:07:53.880
I'm not exactly unrelated here, after all.

01:07:53.880 --> 01:07:57.970
Reinhard isn't the head
of the Astrea family.

01:07:58.400 --> 01:08:03.150
Our lifeline is in this old man's hands.

01:08:03.820 --> 01:08:06.690
Finally caught up, eh?

01:08:06.690 --> 01:08:08.270
Yep, that's right.

01:08:08.270 --> 01:08:11.320
I'm the Astrea family head.

01:08:11.320 --> 01:08:16.910
I never intended to pass it on to Reinhard,
and I never will.

01:08:20.650 --> 01:08:22.910
Lady Felt, I...

01:08:22.910 --> 01:08:24.000
Reinhard.

01:08:24.530 --> 01:08:27.420
Shut up and keep your head up.

01:08:29.040 --> 01:08:30.130
Of course.

01:08:30.570 --> 01:08:31.960
Say whatever you want.

01:08:31.960 --> 01:08:36.470
You're right to feel threatened,
oh great master of Reinhard.

01:08:36.470 --> 01:08:41.310
The Astrea family's mine,
and I won't be backing you.

01:08:41.690 --> 01:08:44.390
- I'm supporting...
- Commoner.

01:08:44.390 --> 01:08:46.980
What is it, Miss Priscilla?

01:08:46.980 --> 01:08:48.810
I'm in the middle of an impor—

01:08:48.810 --> 01:08:50.110
Silence.

01:08:58.200 --> 01:09:00.870
That's enough of your tantrum, Princess.

01:09:01.990 --> 01:09:04.120
C'mon, gimme a break.

01:09:04.120 --> 01:09:06.580
You even drew the Sun Blade!
Almost gave me a heart—

01:09:08.660 --> 01:09:11.630
Schult, carry this commoner out of here.

01:09:11.630 --> 01:09:13.250
You may tend to his wounds.

01:09:13.750 --> 01:09:15.760
Yes, Lady Priscilla!

01:09:16.380 --> 01:09:19.260
Please excuse me, Lord Heinkel!

01:09:19.700 --> 01:09:21.970
Heave-ho... Heave-ho...

01:09:21.970 --> 01:09:25.310
Schult's lively as ever.
Heave-ho... Heave-ho...

01:09:25.800 --> 01:09:28.810
So, was the old guy serious just now?

01:09:28.810 --> 01:09:31.520
Is he gonna drive us out
and take back his seat as lord?

01:09:31.520 --> 01:09:34.730
And if that were true,
what exactly would you do about it?

01:09:34.730 --> 01:09:37.900
Bow out gracefully
with tears in your eyes?

01:09:37.900 --> 01:09:40.660
Ha! Don't make me laugh!

01:09:40.660 --> 01:09:44.620
No matter what anyone says,
that's one thing I'll never do!

01:09:45.200 --> 01:09:48.960
I'll just let this guy make that old man
hand over the inheritance.

01:09:49.350 --> 01:09:53.920
Very well.
My victory is inevitable regardless.

01:09:53.920 --> 01:09:57.970
You might as well color my path
with turmoil for my amusement.

01:09:58.340 --> 01:09:59.930
Yes, fan my flames!

01:09:59.930 --> 01:10:03.390
That is the role destiny
has decreed for you!

01:10:03.390 --> 01:10:07.180
I'll make you cry
and regret that arrogance.

01:10:10.100 --> 01:10:12.730
Damn it! I've gotta calm down.

01:10:12.730 --> 01:10:15.650
I'm the one who lost
his temper back then...

01:10:15.650 --> 01:10:18.190
Don't take it out on the floor.

01:10:18.190 --> 01:10:20.490
You'll trouble the inn workers.

01:10:20.490 --> 01:10:23.490
I'm the only one who blew up back there.

01:10:23.910 --> 01:10:26.580
Everyone else was calm.
I'm pathetic.

01:10:26.580 --> 01:10:33.630
No, your outburst allowed the others
to remain composed.

01:10:33.630 --> 01:10:36.130
Your rashness can come in handy sometimes.

01:10:36.130 --> 01:10:39.800
You're not really trying
to praise me, are you?

01:10:39.800 --> 01:10:42.340
It is true that your actions
were not commendable

01:10:42.340 --> 01:10:45.010
if one were to seek knightly conduct.

01:10:45.480 --> 01:10:46.350
However...

01:10:50.180 --> 01:10:52.390
The heck are you doing?

01:10:52.390 --> 01:10:55.480
As you can see,
I am showing my gratitude.

01:10:55.950 --> 01:11:00.570
Your righteous indignation
was much appreciated.

01:11:02.400 --> 01:11:04.870
You're thanking me
for getting angry in your place?

01:11:04.870 --> 01:11:05.870
Screw off.

01:11:05.870 --> 01:11:08.790
Why would I be mad on your behalf?

01:11:08.790 --> 01:11:11.500
I got pissed because I was fed up.

01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:15.330
If you were ticked off too,
you should've just gotten mad yourself!

01:11:17.920 --> 01:11:21.920
Even if I did, I cannot afford to be
disrespectful to my direct superior.

01:11:21.920 --> 01:11:24.510
How rigid can you be, man?

01:11:24.510 --> 01:11:29.220
Does your heart wear
your knightly shining armor too?

01:11:29.220 --> 01:11:32.010
My heart is clad in armor, you say?

01:11:33.350 --> 01:11:35.190
That is so accurate, it almost hurts.

01:11:36.440 --> 01:11:38.190
Looking at his ugly mug,

01:11:38.190 --> 01:11:40.860
don't tell me he used his influence
as the Sword Saint's dad

01:11:40.860 --> 01:11:42.780
to land that position?

01:11:43.290 --> 01:11:44.700
That is part of it.

01:11:45.270 --> 01:11:47.070
However, the main reason

01:11:47.070 --> 01:11:49.740
lies not with the vice captain,
but because of Reinhard,

01:11:50.350 --> 01:11:53.120
or more accurately, the Astrea family.

01:11:53.580 --> 01:11:58.840
That man is Wilhelm's son
and the current head of the Astrea family.

01:11:59.400 --> 01:12:04.300
What would happen if such an individual
would rebel due to discourteous treatment?

01:12:04.800 --> 01:12:07.970
You're saying that if he feels like it,

01:12:07.970 --> 01:12:10.890
he could turn the Sword Saint's family
against the Kingdom?

01:12:10.890 --> 01:12:17.480
You're telling me the Kingdom
doesn't trust Reinhard and Wilhelm?!

01:12:17.480 --> 01:12:18.610
Fifteen years ago,

01:12:18.610 --> 01:12:22.320
a member of the royal family
was abducted from the palace.

01:12:22.320 --> 01:12:23.940
What about it?

01:12:23.940 --> 01:12:27.740
Back then, Lord Wilhelm
was the captain of the Royal Guard

01:12:27.740 --> 01:12:31.280
and was also responsible for the search
for the kidnapped royalty.

01:12:32.010 --> 01:12:35.370
The former Sword Saint's expedition
against the White Whale took place

01:12:35.370 --> 01:12:40.210
while Lord Wilhelm was away
from the capital to search for the child.

01:12:40.750 --> 01:12:44.460
He couldn't be there for his wife's death
because of the search.

01:12:44.460 --> 01:12:47.220
So you're saying he's holding
a grudge because of that?

01:12:47.740 --> 01:12:49.930
He's not that kind of person!

01:12:49.930 --> 01:12:53.140
Why can't anyone understand that?

01:12:53.140 --> 01:12:54.310
I apologize.

01:12:54.310 --> 01:12:58.400
I shouldn't have brought this up
when you weren't emotionally prepared.

01:12:58.930 --> 01:13:01.940
Even I can tell you're worried
about Reinhard,

01:13:01.940 --> 01:13:04.190
so it's only natural you'd be ticked.

01:13:04.190 --> 01:13:06.240
There's nothing strange about that.

01:13:06.950 --> 01:13:08.610
I've told you before, right?

01:13:08.610 --> 01:13:14.200
You don't need to obsess over being
a well-mannered knight all the time.

01:13:16.290 --> 01:13:20.250
You can take off your armor
and just be Juli sometimes.

01:13:20.250 --> 01:13:24.960
Maybe being flexible would help you
do a lot of things better.

01:13:26.630 --> 01:13:28.630
Juli, you say...

01:13:31.430 --> 01:13:34.990
You've brought up quite a nostalgic name.

01:13:36.390 --> 01:13:38.520
So this is how Juli feels,

01:13:38.520 --> 01:13:41.610
when he's looking up to the sky
and feeling the breeze.

01:13:43.190 --> 01:13:47.940
Now that I think about it,
the sky looked different back then too.

01:13:49.200 --> 01:13:50.660
I don't get you at all.

01:13:51.080 --> 01:13:52.700
Quit showing off, smug bastard.

01:13:56.700 --> 01:13:57.950
Hey, Subaru.

01:13:58.390 --> 01:14:01.120
You looked like you were
really getting along with Julius.

01:14:01.120 --> 01:14:02.460
What were you talking about?

01:14:02.460 --> 01:14:07.840
You're really wrong about that,
but what do you think our topic was?

01:14:09.720 --> 01:14:11.720
Where to play next time, I guess?

01:14:11.720 --> 01:14:12.970
We're not school buddies!

01:14:12.970 --> 01:14:16.220
We were just scouting out the enemy a bit.

01:14:16.220 --> 01:14:19.100
Plus a bit of chitchat, I guess.

01:14:19.100 --> 01:14:21.390
Isn't that what friends do?

01:14:21.390 --> 01:14:23.310
Well, we're definitely not friends.

01:14:23.310 --> 01:14:25.400
That's one thing I'm sure of.

01:14:25.400 --> 01:14:27.860
- So stubborn...
- He really is, I suppose!

01:14:30.110 --> 01:14:32.450
It looks really lively over there!

01:14:32.450 --> 01:14:34.160
So it would seem.

01:14:34.160 --> 01:14:37.580
It feels much louder than yesterday,
I suppose.

01:14:49.630 --> 01:14:51.630
Priscilla?!

01:14:52.510 --> 01:14:54.260
That was a wonderful dance!

01:14:54.260 --> 01:14:58.890
Seeing such amazing footwork like
that almost made my eyes pop out!

01:14:58.890 --> 01:15:03.520
Your performance
was entertaining, as well.

01:15:03.520 --> 01:15:07.320
It has been a while
since a musician has amused me so.

01:15:07.320 --> 01:15:08.610
My time was well spent.

01:15:09.690 --> 01:15:11.240
Oh dear, dearest me,

01:15:11.240 --> 01:15:15.950
could this be Master Natsuki, Lady Emilia,
and the Little Mistress I see?

01:15:18.200 --> 01:15:21.710
Things went crazy,
and I couldn't keep my promise yesterday,

01:15:21.710 --> 01:15:24.260
so it's really good you're here today.

01:15:25.660 --> 01:15:29.340
You have been staring at me
for quite some time now.

01:15:29.340 --> 01:15:30.420
How uncouth!

01:15:30.420 --> 01:15:31.970
I'm sorry!

01:15:31.970 --> 01:15:35.510
I just thought it was really unexpected
for you to start dancing.

01:15:35.510 --> 01:15:39.010
I only dance when the mood strikes me.

01:15:39.010 --> 01:15:43.520
This artist's song
was simply that alluring.

01:15:43.520 --> 01:15:46.980
For real? So you're a Liliana fan, too?

01:15:48.190 --> 01:15:51.690
Are you saying my song
was that amazing?

01:15:51.690 --> 01:15:53.610
Wow, you're making me blush!

01:15:53.610 --> 01:15:56.320
Your song was of great value.

01:15:56.320 --> 01:16:00.490
What say you join me as my songstress?

01:16:00.490 --> 01:16:04.500
Hey, thanks! I'm honored
you think that way about me!

01:16:04.500 --> 01:16:06.710
I'm so flattered!

01:16:06.710 --> 01:16:08.630
But! But!

01:16:09.110 --> 01:16:10.840
I must respectfully decline!

01:16:11.800 --> 01:16:15.130
Oh? And what reason would you have
to refuse my invitation?

01:16:15.750 --> 01:16:18.350
I am Liliana, the bard.

01:16:18.800 --> 01:16:22.770
I am but a wanderer,
destined to be whisked away by the wind.

01:16:22.770 --> 01:16:27.310
I cannot be bound by one land or person.

01:16:27.310 --> 01:16:29.060
It is my way of life.

01:16:29.060 --> 01:16:32.400
And so you decline my invitation?

01:16:32.820 --> 01:16:36.280
My mother, her mother,
and her mother's mother...

01:16:36.280 --> 01:16:38.370
It was the same for my entire clan.

01:16:38.970 --> 01:16:44.620
Our clan leaves nothing behind,
save for our songs in people's hearts.

01:16:44.620 --> 01:16:46.830
Just as a single fence
cannot stop the winds,

01:16:47.340 --> 01:16:51.040
no person can keep us from singing.

01:16:55.300 --> 01:16:56.470
Prisc—

01:16:56.880 --> 01:16:59.390
Very well.
Your resolve is commendable.

01:16:59.390 --> 01:17:02.180
Forgive me, for it was I who was rude.

01:17:02.180 --> 01:17:06.940
Oh, don't be like that!
I'm sorry I couldn't accept.

01:17:07.430 --> 01:17:08.900
What is it, peasant?

01:17:09.900 --> 01:17:11.940
I was just surprised.

01:17:11.940 --> 01:17:17.030
I was sure you'd slice Liliana in half
for rejecting your invitation.

01:17:17.030 --> 01:17:19.610
I was a bit surprised, too.

01:17:19.610 --> 01:17:22.780
I thought you were the type of person

01:17:22.780 --> 01:17:25.250
who'd do everything
to get what you wanted.

01:17:26.250 --> 01:17:28.960
Everything in this world is mine.

01:17:29.420 --> 01:17:33.210
As such, there is no need to keep
all that is beautiful, noble,

01:17:33.210 --> 01:17:37.720
or valuable within my reach to admire.

01:17:37.720 --> 01:17:40.720
As this entire world is my garden,

01:17:40.720 --> 01:17:44.930
it matters not where the singing birds
choose to serenade me.

01:17:46.890 --> 01:17:51.400
Now, now, now!
Now that everyone's calmed down,

01:17:51.400 --> 01:17:55.030
how about I sing you a song
in honor of our friendship?

01:17:55.370 --> 01:17:58.070
And after the song,
we'll have a pleasant chat!

01:17:58.070 --> 01:18:00.360
Now, wouldn't it be nice
if you prepared us

01:18:00.360 --> 01:18:03.660
some snacks for that, Mr. Natsuki?

01:18:05.160 --> 01:18:08.960
Now, wouldn't it be nice
if you prepared us

01:18:08.960 --> 01:18:11.920
some snacks for that, Mr. Natsuki?

01:18:11.920 --> 01:18:12.830
What's this?

01:18:12.830 --> 01:18:16.300
One of those RPG choices
where the dialogue loops until you pick "yes"?

01:18:19.340 --> 01:18:22.010
Man, I really am a pushover.

01:18:22.010 --> 01:18:23.390
Whoops.

01:18:23.390 --> 01:18:27.600
Hey, now.
Shouldn't you be apologizing, bro?

01:18:27.600 --> 01:18:29.640
Why don't you show me some sinc—

01:18:29.640 --> 01:18:31.140
Oh, it's just you, Chin.

01:18:31.140 --> 01:18:33.020
Stop callin' me Chin, damn it!

01:18:33.020 --> 01:18:35.110
The hell are you doin' here?!

01:18:35.110 --> 01:18:37.110
Hey, don't be like that.

01:18:37.110 --> 01:18:39.520
We're pals who've gone through
life and death together!

01:18:39.520 --> 01:18:42.030
When the hell did that happen?! Back off!

01:18:42.030 --> 01:18:44.530
C'mon, hear me out! The thing is—

01:18:44.530 --> 01:18:48.040
Just cut it out already!
Why're you so damn clingy?!

01:18:48.040 --> 01:18:52.000
To everyone whose conversations
and busy schedules I've interrupted...

01:18:52.700 --> 01:18:54.330
- The hell?
- Is something going on?

01:18:54.950 --> 01:18:57.300
I'm sorry for bothering you!

01:18:57.300 --> 01:19:01.800
Please, allow me
but a brief moment of your time!

01:19:02.340 --> 01:19:04.260
Thank you, and I'm sorry!

01:19:04.670 --> 01:19:08.060
I am the Archbishop of Wrath
of the Witch Cult...

01:19:08.700 --> 01:19:11.980
Sirius Romanée-Conti, at your service!

01:19:13.320 --> 01:19:15.400
What did she just say?

01:19:15.400 --> 01:19:17.730
This is a joke right?
I mean, the Witch Cult...

01:19:17.730 --> 01:19:19.480
Hey, did you hear that?!

01:19:19.480 --> 01:19:22.320
Yeah, if this is a joke, it's not funny...

01:19:24.240 --> 01:19:25.740
Okay, that's quite enough!

01:19:25.740 --> 01:19:29.700
It took you thirty five seconds
to quiet down.

01:19:29.700 --> 01:19:33.080
But thank you
for quieting down! I'm sorry!

01:19:33.080 --> 01:19:36.750
I am so overflowing with joy!

01:19:36.750 --> 01:19:43.760
And you, and you over there,
and you two misters over there, I'm sorry!

01:19:43.760 --> 01:19:45.470
Please don't be so angry!

01:19:45.470 --> 01:19:50.930
I am so ashamed to have stolen
your precious time!

01:19:50.930 --> 01:19:54.350
So I'm sorry from the bottom
of my heart! Thank you!

01:19:56.560 --> 01:19:58.400
My, thank you!

01:19:58.400 --> 01:20:01.990
It looks like everyone's calmed down!

01:20:01.990 --> 01:20:03.740
I understand your anxiety.

01:20:03.740 --> 01:20:07.410
But there was something
I just had to confirm,

01:20:07.410 --> 01:20:10.870
so I had to partake
in some of your precious time!

01:20:10.870 --> 01:20:13.370
Confirm... something...?

01:20:13.370 --> 01:20:16.330
I'm sorry! Please don't be so noisy!

01:20:16.330 --> 01:20:18.420
If there's something wrong,
please tell me!

01:20:18.420 --> 01:20:22.880
I'll do my best to answer
for everyone's sake!

01:20:22.880 --> 01:20:26.510
Okay, I'll take you up on your offer.

01:20:26.510 --> 01:20:30.350
Ah, yes! Yes, good sir! Thank you!

01:20:30.730 --> 01:20:32.810
I don't know what you want,

01:20:32.810 --> 01:20:36.270
but I've got some girls
waiting for me, four at that!

01:20:36.270 --> 01:20:40.690
So can you get this over with
and let us go already?

01:20:40.690 --> 01:20:43.860
Oh my! That's horrible! I'm sorry!

01:20:43.860 --> 01:20:46.740
But you're quite the sly one,
aren't you, good sir?

01:20:46.740 --> 01:20:50.160
Leaving four girls waiting like that,
now that's just naughty!

01:20:50.160 --> 01:20:53.700
But thank you. I'm sorry.
I'm going to hurry now.

01:20:53.700 --> 01:20:58.920
Nah, it's fine! Let's have a nice
and calm conversation, alright?

01:20:59.320 --> 01:21:01.880
I'm sorry you needed to be considerate,
but thank you!

01:21:01.880 --> 01:21:04.380
Now, let's get straight to the point!

01:21:04.380 --> 01:21:07.880
It's time to unveil
why I have appeared before you!

01:21:09.590 --> 01:21:12.680
Didn't you say you wanted
to check something with us?

01:21:12.680 --> 01:21:14.600
So, what is it?

01:21:14.600 --> 01:21:16.890
Right! Come on, tell us!

01:21:16.890 --> 01:21:20.610
Hurry up or I'll be late for work!

01:21:21.690 --> 01:21:24.940
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm really sorry!

01:21:24.940 --> 01:21:27.490
I'll get this over right away!

01:21:27.490 --> 01:21:31.160
You see, what I want to confirm is...

01:21:31.160 --> 01:21:36.290
Frankly speaking, love.

01:21:36.290 --> 01:21:37.910
Wah, I'm so embarrassed!

01:21:39.850 --> 01:21:45.590
Would you be so kind as to accompany me
in confirming my love?

01:21:45.590 --> 01:21:46.550
Sure!

01:21:46.550 --> 01:21:48.590
- Yeah!
- Of course!

01:21:48.590 --> 01:21:52.800
Really? Thank you, thank you! I'm sorry!

01:21:52.800 --> 01:21:54.930
Ah, yes, the world really is kind!

01:21:54.930 --> 01:21:57.730
So full of love and kindness!

01:21:57.730 --> 01:22:01.980
I'm so grateful
I get to savor a feeling like this!

01:22:01.980 --> 01:22:04.820
To permit and yield to one another!

01:22:04.820 --> 01:22:08.820
That is why I say not only "thank you,"

01:22:08.820 --> 01:22:10.280
but "I'm sorry" too.

01:22:18.200 --> 01:22:20.040
Now, take a look.

01:22:20.040 --> 01:22:22.250
I've kept you waiting for too long.

01:22:22.880 --> 01:22:24.570
I'm sorry.

01:22:25.610 --> 01:22:27.050
I'm sorry it's so tight!

01:22:27.050 --> 01:22:30.380
But a brave boy like
you shouldn't be crying, yes?

01:22:30.380 --> 01:22:34.390
I wanted to keep this to myself,
but now that you've wet yourself,

01:22:34.390 --> 01:22:37.390
everyone knows your shame!

01:22:37.390 --> 01:22:39.850
She's right! That's so embarrassing!

01:22:39.850 --> 01:22:42.520
You're a brave boy, right? Tough it out!

01:22:42.520 --> 01:22:46.650
A man can only cry
three times in his life, you know!

01:22:49.190 --> 01:22:55.620
He might be cowering right now,
but he really is brave boy!

01:22:56.160 --> 01:22:59.080
This is Lusbel Callard.

01:22:59.080 --> 01:23:03.710
A nine-year-old boy living in Pristella!

01:23:03.710 --> 01:23:06.340
My, he has such
a bright future ahead of him!

01:23:06.340 --> 01:23:13.180
Now, young Lusbel has
an adorable childhood friend named Tina.

01:23:13.180 --> 01:23:17.760
They care so deeply for each other,
an ideal relationship, I'd call it.

01:23:17.760 --> 01:23:22.810
And so I spent a long time
mulling over who to bring here.

01:23:22.810 --> 01:23:25.940
At first, I was thinking
of bringing little Tina here,

01:23:25.940 --> 01:23:29.980
but young Lusbel asked me
so hard to take him instead.

01:23:29.980 --> 01:23:33.280
I was so moved.

01:23:33.280 --> 01:23:39.490
And so I yielded to his enthusiasm
and decided to cooperate with him!

01:23:41.500 --> 01:23:44.290
Stop crying, Lusbel! You're amazing!

01:23:44.290 --> 01:23:47.000
If you're gonna be a man,
be a man until the end!

01:23:47.000 --> 01:23:49.460
You're going to grow up
into a wonderful man!

01:23:49.460 --> 01:23:52.470
Lusbel! Pristella's pride and joy!

01:23:53.720 --> 01:23:58.850
Ah, ah! Thank you! Thank you!

01:23:58.850 --> 01:24:01.520
Ah, this world is so wonderful!

01:24:01.520 --> 01:24:03.430
You all understand!

01:24:03.430 --> 01:24:05.900
After all, his actions are truly

01:24:05.900 --> 01:24:08.360
love itself!

01:24:10.320 --> 01:24:12.780
Thank you, Sirius!

01:24:12.780 --> 01:24:16.000
Thank you... thank you...!

01:24:19.580 --> 01:24:22.330
Rifts are born
when we don't know one another!

01:24:22.330 --> 01:24:26.080
Conflict arises
when we don't understand each other!

01:24:26.080 --> 01:24:30.040
And if we give up on one another because
of our differences, bonds can't be forged!

01:24:30.040 --> 01:24:33.760
Now, how are your hearts right now?

01:24:33.760 --> 01:24:35.260
Stop underestimatin' us!

01:24:35.260 --> 01:24:39.640
- We'll never give up on one another!
- Our hearts are one!

01:24:39.640 --> 01:24:42.180
Thank you! Thank you!

01:24:42.180 --> 01:24:45.560
Is everyone filled with joy right now?!

01:24:45.560 --> 01:24:46.890
Damn right we are!

01:24:46.890 --> 01:24:48.860
I've never felt so happy before!

01:24:48.860 --> 01:24:52.980
- Thank you, Lusbel!
- Thank you, Sirius!

01:25:10.840 --> 01:25:13.920
Look how they praise your courage,
young Lusbel!

01:25:15.990 --> 01:25:18.180
Yes, there truly was love!

01:25:18.180 --> 01:25:20.850
There truly was love here!

01:25:20.850 --> 01:25:25.730
Everyone's hearts have become one!

01:25:27.520 --> 01:25:30.980
Yes! A thousand rounds of applause!

01:25:38.450 --> 01:25:41.870
Ah, this world is so kind!

01:25:52.380 --> 01:25:54.960
And after the song,
we'll have a pleasant chat!

01:25:55.480 --> 01:25:57.420
Now, wouldn't it be nice
if you prepared us

01:25:57.420 --> 01:26:00.890
some snacks for that, Mr. Natsuki?

01:26:03.850 --> 01:26:06.180
Err, is something wrong?

01:26:06.180 --> 01:26:08.310
Hello? Are you ignoring me?

01:26:08.820 --> 01:26:12.360
Hey! Heeey!

01:26:12.360 --> 01:26:13.270
Hey!
I feel sick.

01:26:13.270 --> 01:26:13.940
Hey!

01:26:13.940 --> 01:26:16.320
Subaru?! What happened?!

01:26:16.320 --> 01:26:17.860
Is something the matter, I wonder?

01:26:18.360 --> 01:26:19.610
Subaru? Subaru!

01:26:19.610 --> 01:26:20.820
I feel sick...

01:26:22.200 --> 01:26:23.530
I feel sick...

01:26:26.600 --> 01:26:28.660
THEATRICAL MALICE
I feel sick...!

01:26:28.660 --> 01:26:30.960
THEATRICAL MALICE
